INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (25, 3, N'Works in multiple areas of Surgical Services assisting with the clerical needs of the department.
In all areas, projects a positive, calm, professional and helpful demeanor to patients, visitors, staff and physicians.
Demonstrates positive effective communication skills, maintaining required level of confidentiality, report and convey patient information effectively with all members of the healthcare team and families.
Works effectively as a team member, and adapts to constant changes in the workload.
Demonstrates good organizational skills with the ability to multitask in an efficient manner within the entire work area.
Demonstrates effective computer skills, including changing patient status, order entry and retrieval, and other skills as necessary.
Demonstrates proficiency in scheduling elective procedures for Surgical Services. Ability to coordinate scheduled procedure with appropriate room assignment, equipment required, and contact vendor for special needs, supplies, and equipment. Prepares surgical schedule, and coordinates with ASU, PAT, Registration, and Interventional Radiology.
Works effectively at the Ambulatory Surgery Front desk, demonstrating a professional demeanor greeting patient and family, providing assistance with concerns encountered by patient and family. Notify appropriate unit of patient arrival, inform family members  use of information board and beeper. Directs, and/or escort family member to appropriate location, provide for comfort measures if needed. Collaborates with all departments of Surgical Services relaying accurate information to visitors, staff, and physicians utilizing rounding procedure in atrium and unit desk to provide additional updates to patients, family, and health care providers.
Demonstrates proficiency in assembling charts, assisting with changes in the surgical schedule, patient arrival, and other clerical duties when working in ASU/PAT. Collaborates with PAT staff, ASU Charge Nurse coordinating changes to the surgical schedule.
Acts as a liaison between staff, physicians, and other departments.
Acts as a liaison between patients and their families and staff informing the patient and families of delays and patient location and informing the staff of patient and family needs.
Correct identified discern report issues. Obtain CPOE orders, History & Physicals from physician offices.
Prompt fax retrievals and distribution.
Maintains departmental logs on a daily basis.
Acts as a preceptor for new employees.', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:08.0366667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:08.0366667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (26, 4, N'Contribute to the planning, organizing, management and research of potential sponsors and GIK donors for special events with the Resource Development Manager, including Foundation team and event committees.
Assist in digital content, prize coordination and event day set-up and breakdown.
Assists with scheduling event volunteers and responsibilities.
Manages registration logistics for each signature event, including requesting tables for set up, volunteer training, and day-of management of volunteers and vendors.
Manage on-site registration at all signature events, including pre-event logistics and real-time customer service needs. Ensure registration table staff are efficiently trained and that the registration process is a continuously improving system through feedback sessions, technological improvements, etc.
Manage and update each event’s guest submissions process and forms. During event lead up, manages guest change process and acts as point of contact for Foundation team questions relating to guest management.
Manages ticket sales for accuracy and confirmation of payment, capturing ticket holder’s information for follow-up, registration list or seating chart. data entry into Raisers Edge for event attendees.
Manages signature event program book donor listings and collaborates with Foundation team for review and edits.
As directed by the Resource Development Manager, manage all printing needs relating to event management, including program, signage, etc.
Manage tax receipt mailings by coordinating weekly reviews of donor contributions for signature events.
Oversee event email inbox communication and ensure timely responses to donor inquiries and RSVPs.
Maintains signature event voicemail boxes and responds to donor inquiries.
Maintain and continuously evaluate template documents used for events, including fundraising materials, acknowledgement letters, tax receipts, confirmation letters, etc.
Coordinate tabling events, including dates, securing location, materials to market special event, volunteers to assist, set up and breakdown of tabling events.
Work collaboratively with the Foundation team to maintain a healthy, professional, and vibrant working relationship within the office and across the institution. Support new ideas and creative development of events under supervision of the Resource Development Manager.
Flexible to work nights or weekends as needed for major special events.', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:10.1000000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:10.1000000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (27, 5, N'Prepares monthly billing statements for Private Division.  Researches all types of Explanation of Benefits (EOB’s) for proper processing of claims.
Balances weekly and monthly billing for CCE/ADI contracts.
Prepares Medicaid claims for electronic transmission and enters into Web Portal for transmitting.  Retrieves electronic EOB’s as necessary. Verifies Medicaid eligibility.
Processes all authorizations received for Insurance and Medicaid claims into patient accounts for Private division and non-PPS claims for certified division. Obtain authorization on all Medicaid hourly and visit patients.
Posts transactions from weekly time slips to patient accounts to create payroll reports. Audits Horizon payroll reports before sending to hospital payroll dept.
Manages Accounts Receivable Aging for all accounts billed by researching and re-filing claims as well as generating reminder statements and delinquent calls to patients for Private division.
Prepares deposits and posts payments to patient accounts accordingly.  Works with PFS for bank processing.  Maintains cash receipts spreadsheets for accurate monthly deposit totals.
Checks Common Working File to verify Medicare coverage on new/pending patients daily.  Establishes correct episode sequence in Event Manager from data found in CWF.
Works with CBO to research Medicare Certified agency denials and any billing issues not handled by CBO.
Prepares Horizon data reports as requested for Medicare Agency and Private Agency.  Prepares HCS month end   reports for all divisions and forwards to FHW Accounting next business day after CBO close.
Continual involvement in improving accuracy and timeliness of Home Care Services financial processes.
Covers for front line phone duties.
Covers for Payroll Coordinator.
Acts as Home Care software, SuperUser and resource for other users.
Assists Intake in Medicare Certified Agency, in verifying benefits and entering data into Horizon as schedule permits.
Other duties and special projects as assigned.', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:12.1600000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:12.1600000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (28, 6, N'Assists staff pharmacists to resolve ""problem orders""
Assists with intradepartmental in-services provided to meet TJC requirements for training and education
Collects and assesses performance improvement activities documentation for use in managerial decisions
Designs and implements programs for enhancing the clinical role of other pharmacists
Develops, monitors and reports medication usage activities
Documents problem, goal, progress, and outcome on interdisciplinary notes
Ensures clinical activities are performed daily
Establishes education programs that enable other pharmacists to perform clinical and pharmacy care activities
Member of the Corporate Clinical Pharmacy Committee
Performs therapeutic drug level monitoring
Provides drug information to hospital and medical staff upon request
Provides educational publications to physicians and other healthcare personnel, as appropriate or when requested
Recommends and develops programs designed to provide the best therapeutic drug usage in the most cost-effective manner
Recommends and helps develop programs designed to improve patient outcomes
Reports hazards and adverse occurrences via the proper risk management channels
Responsible for nursing in-services as requested by director or Nursing education
Responsible for follow-up/closure of own clinical notes
Reviews and recommends various drug acquisition options during shortages or outages
Reviews Clinical Data reports, consulting with prescriber as necessary
Reviews patient''s medication regimen for drug-drug and drug-food interactions and possible allergies
Rounds in ICU reviewing patients drug therapy regimen
Understands and maintains performance improvement activities and TJC requirements
Works cooperatively with all members of the hospital team
Document interventions in Theradoc for corporate accountabilities
Coordination of the overall activities of the Clinical Pharmacist Specialists in order to maximize productivity in hospital service
Coordination/approval of pharmacy practice experience schedules (i.e. weekends, order perfection, operational support, other contemporary issues)
Coordination/approval of pharmacy service coverage schedules
Coordinate emergency coverage upon request (computer down time, sick calls, staff shortage, regulatory inspections etc.,)
Evaluate the need for additional infrastructure and resources necessary to meet the clinical service goals for Pharmacy Services as is appropriate
Coordinate the completion of Performance Evaluations for Clinical Pharmacist Specialists Initial, Midpoint, and Final—in conjunction with Education Coordinator and appropriate Director
Partner with the Education Coordinator to integrate initiatives and activities of the hospital/clinics and College of Pharmacy as appropriate
Provide guidance regarding appropriate expenditure of time and resources for each Clinical Pharmacist Specialist (particularly with regard to engagement in pharmacy practice experience)
Scope of Pharmacy committee membership
P & T Committee membership and coordination as assigned
Coordinate recruitment of Clinical Pharmacist Specialists
Participates in University preceptor programs and actively precepts pharmacy students and residents throughout the year
Provide clinical pharmacy services, including primary and consultative services, to health care providers and patients to ensure optimal drug utilization in assigned specialty area(s)
Participate in clinical research as assigned
Responsible for compounding and dispensing medications and parenteral admixtures in accordance with established Federal and State regulations and accreditation standards
Effectively verify patient medication orders for appropriateness and accuracy
Provide education and training to pharmacy students, medical staff physicians and nurses, and healthcare-related professionals
Prioritize level of care based on critical needs
Participate in interdisciplinary patient care rounds and communicate follow-up with clinical team
Prevent, detect, and resolve medication-related problems and to make appropriate evidence-based, patient-centered medication therapy recommendations as part of the interdisciplinary team
Determine and resolve any medication therapy problems including drugs without indications, medical conditions for which no therapy is prescribed, therapy inappropriate for medical condition, incomplete immunization record, inappropriate dose, dosage form, duration, schedule, route of administration, method of administration, therapeutic duplication, medication allergies, and clinically significant drug, drug-disease, drug-nutrient, or drug-laboratory test interactions
Appropriately document clinical interventions
Appropriately complete Interdisciplinary Plans of Care (IPOC) as assigned
Participate in opportunities to improve the quality, effectiveness, and/or efficiency in distributing medications to our customers and patients
Provide concise, applicable, comprehensive, and timely responses to requests for drug information from patients and health care providers
Provide and document discharge medication teaching upon request
Participate with Director of Pharmacy, clinical team and the Pharmacy department to evaluate and measure the impact of new approaches that have been implemented.
Identify high-cost and high-use agents within defined area of practice and participates in financial management initiatives (revenue generating, cost containment, etc)
Report medication errors and adverse drug reactions
Support the Mission, Vision and Values of the Department of Pharmacy
Provide clinical pharmacy services directed to the general population of the facility
Provides at least one (1) Pharmacy staff development initiative per year
The pharmacist shall provide accurate and clinically relevant drug information to physicians, nurses, and other health care providers upon request in accordance with their expertise to do so
Participates in mentorship and professional development of pharmacists, technicians, pharmacy residents, and pharmacy students
Participate collegially in the development of new programs, services, and practices, educational activities of the pharmacy department and medical team
Consistently attend pharmacy student/residency seminars and presentations.
Adhere to the facility formulary by assisting in recommending formulary changes to physicians and developing clinical programs to promote appropriate, cost-effective prescribing
Actively participates in the development and implementation of performance/quality improvement and patient safety activities for clinical service area, Pharmacy, and facility
Design and assist in Provider education and drug awareness programs, provide clinical support to the Pharmaceutical Services team.
Performs other duties as assigned', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:14.0766667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:14.0766667' AS DateTime2))
