INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (174, 40, N'Pharmacy Operations

Actively performs all pharmacy technician functions and maintains active proficiency in standard work parameters, hospital and pharmacy specific computer systems, and operational programs

Maintains knowledge of operational functions in and actively provides coverage as needed:
•	Central Pharmacy
•	IV Room
•	Delivery
•	Controlled Substances
•	Quality Assurance & Sampling
•	Technician Inventory Check 
•	Medication History 
•	Clinical Services Support
•	Regulatory Compliance 
•	Designated Trainer
•	Quality Assurance Auditing 
•	Non-Sterile Compounding/Repackaging
•	Hazardous Medication Sterile Compounding 
•	Purchasing and Contract Compliance

Oversees appropriate utilization of medication automation, technology, and computer systems
•	Accurately reviews electronic reports
•	Maintains expertise in electronic report processes

Accurately oversees the management of medication inventories and the preparation and delivery of patient‐specific medication doses
•	Manages medication delivery activities
•	Prepares accurate medication products for delivery
•	Prevents improper drug, dose, dosage form selection, expiration dating, and barcode scanning issues when preparing products for final check
•	Performs oral and injectable product compounding if applicable

Supervises technician and intern practice 
•	Maintains competency to perform technician duties and roles as needed
•	Prioritizes workload, organizes workflow, and checks accuracy of pharmacy technician activities 
•	Intervenes as needed to optimize the patient-centered pharmacy services provided in/by practice area

Pharmacy Practice

Supports patient‐centered care services
•	Facilitates medication safety practices by identifying and reporting potential medication errors such as look-alike sound-alike medications
•	Prepares and delivers accurate, safe and timely medication
•	Places practice priority on the delivery of patient‐centered care
•	Partners with pharmacist to improve quality and safety of patient care
•	Provides medication histories as needed

Works as an active member of pharmacy programs and multidisciplinary team 
•	Collaborates with other pharmacy staff 
•	Collaborates with care providers and Pharmacist to optimize care and improve services 

Teamwork and Inter-Professional Collaboration

Presents to assigned areas on time, ready to work and does not exhibit unscheduled absenteeism
•	Adheres to lunch and break schedule and monitors team adherence

Assures continuity of service between shifts, among pharmacy staff assignments, and across pharmacy practice areas
•	Assures appropriate handoff between shifts and facilitates team meetings/huddles
•	Accepts any necessary work from preceding shift and does not leave excessive work for following shift

Works effectively with all members of the healthcare team to ensure the best outcome for the patient
•	Demonstrates sensitivity to the perspective of the patient, caregiver, or health care colleague in all communications
•	Actively supports teammates (pharmacists, technicians, managers)
•	Uses effective negotiation skills to resolve conflicts

Assists pharmacy managers and pharmacists with compliance and auditing

Teaching, Training, Precepting, and Mentorship

Mentors new-staff and assists with training

Supports quality training opportunities and relationships for teaching and precepting 
•	Supports all pharmacist student, pharmacy technician student and resident learning experiences, if applicable
•	Supports current and established staff training experiences and competencies 
•	Determines and validates competency

Demonstrates desire and aptitude for teaching and competency of 
•	The teaching roles: Instructing, Modeling, and Coaching
•	Teaching clinical problem solving 
•	Evaluating experiential performance 
•	Providing criteria-based feedback
•	Teaching independent evidence-based practice
•	Differentiating between students and resident learning experiences, if applicable

Precepts and mentors (number defined annually):
•	Pharmacy technician student rotations

Quality Improvement, Regulatory Compliance, and Accreditation

Supports and participates in medication‐use process improvements led by colleagues and peers

Supports regulatory compliance initiatives and supports institutional accreditation processes

Identifies practice-related issues which require evaluation
•	Identifies the need for quality improvement initiatives or healthcare provider education as needed to advance practice 
•	Identifies short- and long-term obstacles to patient care and medication safety, regulatory compliance, or stewardship of resources


Professional Activities and Practice Advancements

Maintains a commitment to pharmacy practice via participation in pharmacy technician professional activities and practice advancement accomplishments. Supports improvements in and contributions to pharmacy practice

Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching (some examples):
•	Student Evaluations
•	Teaching Awards

Leadership and Organizational Involvement
•	Participates in departmental meetings 
•	Participates in departmental educational activities
•	Supports practice advancement initiatives, clinical research projects, and stewardship initiatives led by colleagues and peers, if applicable
•	Participates in shared governance committee(s), if applicable
•	Maintains professional image
•	Performs other duties as assigned


Schedule and Human Resources Management
Maintains competent, skilled, and cooperative staff by coordinating training for new employees, coaching and mentoring of all employees, and routine professional development for all staff 

Leads recruitment, interview, and hiring processes for staff in assigned areas

Develops a harmonious and satisfied staff by facilitating engagement initiatives and taking actions that appropriately maintain positive employee engagement 

Manages and monitors staff performance in assigned pharmacy areas to ensure accuracy and quality of services, completion of all tasks, and mitigation and correction of deficiencies 

Provides department leadership with feedback regarding job performance including employee discipline if needed and completes performance appraisals for assigned employees 

Develops standards of performance to maximize staff roles in accordance with licensure

Manages schedules and staff requests for PDO and adjusts coverage for sick calls or staff shortages such that department workloads are covered and each area is provided coverage 

Monitors and reports usage of staff overtime, time and attendance deviations, and staff sick calls', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:25.2166667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:25.2166667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (175, 41, N'Performs assigned pre-analytical activities related to laboratory testing, which may include:
Collects patient, physician and test order information in order to create patient accounts. This includes verifying patient identification, insurance information, physician credentials and test order requirements.
Blood specimen collection to include phlebotomy and skin puncture for all age groups
General equipment maintenance, function checks and documentation
Receives, and processes patient specimens which includes separating specimens by centrifugation prior to testing. May include transporting.
Aliquots different sample types, if needed, and either loads preanalytical instruments, which include automated stainers, or delivers them to the testing department
Cytopreparatory staining
Accessioning of surgical cases that requires a knowledge of anatomy.
Receive and set up cultures. Inoculation of different petri dishes for bacterial growth
Blood and/or Blood Component processing, storing, shipping, modifying and selecting compatible products using a validated Transfusion Information System
Performs periodic preventive instrument maintenance and quality assurance procedures as assigned
Cleaning and disinfection of selected or assigned laboratory equipment and spaces, and other pre-analytical activities.
Inventory control and supply stocking
Continually maintains workspaces in a neat, organized, and properly supplied; properly stores documentation and paperwork.
Performs post-analytical activities related to laboratory testing as needed to support assigned department.
Performs various support activities to facilitate operation of assigned department or work area, which may include answering the telephone, clerical and receptionist duties.
Assists the Laboratory management with special projects as assigned.
Assists in teaching new staff and Phlebotomy Students when assigned.
Provides resolution to customer service issues within guidelines and supports education to clinical staff.
Participates in, and has knowledge of, laboratory and hospital Performance Improvement activities, including evaluation of new equipment and/or procedures or methods.
Performs waived testing, and associated, quality control, maintenance, troubleshooting, documentation and result reporting, if applicable
Adheres to the Emplify Corporate Compliance Plan and to all rules and regulations of all applicable local, state, and federal agencies and accrediting bodies; protects confidentiality of patient information and results at all times.
Provides and acts on technical and support information related to the elements of laboratory testing for all age groups, from neo-nates through geriatric patients.
Follows appropriate safety policies including the appropriate use of PPE, handwashing, and hazardous chemical handling.  Demonstrates understanding and adheres to Chemical Hygiene plan and Infection Control policies.  Employee job duties may include transport of hazardous waste from the point of generation to a designated secure storage area; employee will be required to complete initial training (prior to handling hazardous waste) and refresher training to include proper handling and transport of hazardous waste, and proper selection, use and disposal of personal protective equipment.
Performs other duties as assigned or directed to ensure the smooth operation of the department or unit.', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:27.6666667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:27.6666667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (176, 42, N'Assists patients with activities of daily living (ADL)
Provides or assists with providing direct patient care, diagnostic procedures, and therapeutic interventions
Observes and records patient behaviors and activities
Reports changes in patient conditions to appropriate personnel and recommends treatment plan modifications
Establishes therapeutic relationships with assigned patients
Works directly with patients, family members, physicians, and community providers to ensure collaborative and continuous care
May be required to manage daily group activities
Assists patients to perform routine activities of daily living
Recognizes potential escalation of behavior and has ability to use appropriate verbal and physical interventions
Recognizes potential safety hazards, intervenes for the safety of patients, visitors and staff and notifies appropriate department or person for correction of the problem
Assists in restraint situations: utilizing de-escalation skills to prevent restraints, applying restraints when needed with RN direction, maintaining patient safety, appropriate documentation of patient behaviors and interventions
Implements activities in a consistent manner
Adheres to activity calendar and/or program schedule. Demonstrates skills in self-esteem, interpersonal skills, and behavior management
Performs other duties as assigned', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:29.6966667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:29.6966667' AS DateTime2))
