Complete training course and pass Powered Industrial Truck Certification (PIT) requirements
Meet established minimum productivity standards in a fast-paced working environment
Pick, build, and transport a stable pallet of various products
Identify correct supplies and applicable unit of measure
Maintain a quality of work that limits miss-picks, shorts and damages
Confirm the picking of order on the computer or equivalent technology; verify the order; label the containers
Retrieve and transport product to assigned slots
Perform warehouse counts and participate in warehouse inventories
Maintain a clean and neat working environment
Replenish bin locations as needed
Dispose of waste materials
Shrink-wrap pallets
Work flexible shifts, including evenings and weekends, as scheduled
Load Trucks as needed
Provides regular feedback to supervisors and managers on teammate performance
Demonstrates behavior in line with Emplify’s core values
