INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (182, 48, N'Verbalizes knowledge of Hearing Impairment High Risk Factors.
Utilizes proper equipment for the screening situation and sets it up for maximum efficiency in the work space. Completes a weekly inventory to maintain adequate supplies for screenings, as observed by the Hearing Screen Coordinator.
Performs Infant Hearing Screen and correctly reports infant screening results to the Hearing Screen Coordinator. Upon failure of a baby on the initial hearing screening, calls outpatient center and sets appointment for follow-up testing.
Charges patients accurately for services according to the guidelines of the CPT code format and Price File following department guidelines.
Utilizes communication skills appropriate to the population served, which may include: Neonate/Infant (birth < 1), Pediatric (1 < 12 yrs), Adolescent (12 < 18 yrs), Adult (18 < 65 yrs) and Geriatric (65 + yrs).
Participates in practice changes as a result of performance improvements activities. Supports quality standards and initiatives set by the department.
Willingly adjusts to changes in workload by altering work hours to assist at other locations as approved and observed by the Hearing Screen Coordinator.
Practices principles of employee and patient safety when performing daily job activities via observation.
Complies with Emplify Compliance Plan, rules and regulations of all local, state, and federal agencies, and with the standards of all accrediting bodies and payers as evident through documentation reviews, tracers and rounds results', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:39.9666667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:39.9666667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (183, 49, N'Supervises all Imaging support staff
Monitors Departmental efficiency
May perform, analyze & process various computing applications, gathers statistics, works with net revenue & maintains cost of supply items including working patient charge issues
Maintains a knowledge and understanding of the Key Performance Indicators. Suggests and implements opportunities for process improvement in the department as it relates to the Imaging support staff
May use Patient Financial Services (PFS) training to fulfill job functions as needed. Schedules or reschedules patients as needed. Obtains any necessary required financial, historical, clinical or patient information through contact with patient, physician offices or other information providers
Completes support staff duties including but not limited to greeting patients, answering the phone, printing patient records for release internally and externally and faxes paper records always adhering to HIPAA and/or established guidelines. Completes tasks in a timely manner as an example to others within the department. Coaches support staff on the correct techniques to fulfill these everyday job duties
May release CD images/reports to patients and/or physician’s office utilizing proper sign out process. Prints patients’ records for release internally and externally always adhering to HIPAA and/or established guidelines [Records]
Uses functions of computer system, fax machine, copier, digitizer, scanner, and PACS station
Maintains work environment that results in meeting scorecard goals for assigned area. Assists manager in monitoring and reducing over time. Responsible for approving PDO requests and coordinating coverage
Provides individual and team fact-based feedback that motivates and teaches; also provides input and feedback to manager for annual and interim evaluations
Participates in customer service workshops and seminars as recommended by Manager
Assists with budget by monitoring productivity and department expenses', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:42.0666667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:42.0666667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (184, 50, N'Meets call / customer service-centered standards.
Answers and transfers incoming calls both timely and accurately - following call processing procedures
Responds quickly and accurately to all Codes, Alerts, Drills and Testing following proper
procedures
Documents all event details timely and accurately
