INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (203, 67, N'Evaluates outpatient orders, requisitions and laboratory specimens for completeness and accuracy.
Applies knowledge of anatomy and physiology, clinical disease processes, pharmacology, and diagnostic and procedural terminology to determine the appropriate code assignment.
Analyzes medical records, interprets documentation and assigns proper ICD-10, Current Procedural Terminology/HealthCare Common Procedure Coding System (CPT/HCPCS) modifiers, utilizing designated software to include Computer Assisted Coding (CAC) and/or encoder, coding manuals and other coding reference materials as required.
Sequences diagnoses and procedures properly and according to UHDDS definition and in accordance with coding guidelines, policies and procedures.
Reviews and checks outpatient services and test orders to ensure medical necessity was met, utilizing designated software and/or local coverage determination (LCD) policies.
Reviews claim edits and revises coding as appropriate for specific CPT/HCPCS codes.
Seeks clarification from physicians or other staff in cases where documentation is absent, ambiguous, or contradictory. Reviews claims returned from various departments due to edits and processes corrections for clean claim submission or post claim denial review for appeal, working to ensure timely billing.
Assures timely processing or coding of all encounters, consistently reaching department and corporate goals of coding test/service within 4 days of discharge; keeps all accounts under 30 days old.
Abides by the Standards of Ethical Coding as set forth by the American Health Information Management Association (AHIMA) / American Association of Procedural Coders (AAPC) and adheres to official coding guidelines at all times.
Attends coding educational seminars and takes advantage of continuing education opportunities, when available.  Remains knowledgeable in coding guidelines and conventions, staying current with all aspects of outpatient coding.
Assists in training new coders and/or physicians to become acclimated to the environment and in understanding internal coding policies and procedures, and documentation guidelines, as requested.', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:17.9933333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:17.9933333' AS DateTime2))
