Review and approve refunds, write-offs and adjustments on accounts, as defined in Emplify policies
Work collaboratively with other department leadership, including revenue cycle, finance, IT, and physician practice personnel
Utilize knowledge of revenue cycle processes that include insurance claim follow-up, denial management, payment posting, credit resolution, etc.
Utilize knowledge of contractual constraints potentially impacting payer responsibility of adjudication
Achieve superior customer satisfaction by embracing and exemplifying the Emplify service standards
Responsible for other duties as assigned by the Emplify leadership team"', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:58.2733333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:58.2733333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (245, 88, N'" Provide leadership and support to staff responsible for posting activities, including proactive training and guidance, troubleshooting support, issue escalation, and project prioritization
Identify and help resolve problems in the payment posting processes and when appropriate, identifies and initiates change to prevent future problems or improve existing processes
Assist Centralized Payment Posting (CPP) manager in department compliance with established policies and procedures of Emplify and helps ensure that all policies and procedures reflect compliance with government regulations
Collaborate with other CPP supervisors on CPP operational and strategic matters
Develop and maintain an understanding of Federal, State, local and industry regulations, rules, and standards to help ensure compliance with payment posting and refund requirements (CMS, Federal and State legislation, etc.)
Implement and monitor key performance indicators and productivity goals; identify root cause for variances and applicable process improvements; and report key findings to appropriate leadership
Responsible for the establishment and effectiveness of internal controls
Review and approve refunds, write-offs and adjustments on accounts, as defined in Emplify policies
Work collaboratively with other department leadership, including revenue cycle, finance, IT, and physician practice personnel
Utilize knowledge of revenue cycle processes that include insurance claim follow-up, denial management, payment posting, credit resolution, etc.
Achieve superior customer satisfaction by embracing and exemplifying the Emplify service standards
Responsible for other duties as assigned by the Emplify leadership team"', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:24:00.1533333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:24:00.1533333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (246, 89, N'" Lead workstreams on behalf of the Clinical Cabinet working closely with the Executive Sponsors and project teams of Emplify Clinicals strategic initiatives, the ACCO/ SVP, Nursing VP, and market Division VP’s.
Drive development of strategic initiatives by structuring complex issues into phased workstreams and deliverables. Ensure project goals and objectives are achieved within the project scope and timeframe established by the ACCO/SVP and management committees. Develop and lead strategic business value propositions and support the strategic initiatives identified by the Clinical Cabinet and senior executives.
Coordinates agendas by collecting, prioritizing and completing follow-up activities related to agenda items by coordinating and communicating with senior executives and other leaders. Ensures that strategic topics are brought for review in alignment with project timelines.
Serve as an active business partner and leader with the team of executives reporting to the ACCO/CNE and Corporate Nursing Vice President in the execution of the ACCO/CNE’s agenda and strategy and leadership of departments and initiatives.
Coordinates the development of executive level presentations on behalf of the ACCO/CNE and Corporate Nursing Vice President related to the strategic vison of nursing.
Collaborates with ACCO/CNE and Corporate Nursing VP in the development, management and execution of strategic initiatives and projects related to the Nursing strategic plan and 2030 company aspirations.
Works with nursing leaders from all markets to support nursing practices that prioritize patient safety, evidence-based care, and meeting nursing quality care measures.
Collaborates with interdisciplinary market leaders to ensure alignment between nursing care practices and the practices of the interdisciplinary clinical team.
Develops and leads a structure for Nursing Shared Governance  that provides nurses the ability to influence policies and decisions that affect nursing practice at Emplify, including  the creation  of a standard professional practice model that reflects the Mission and Vision of Emplify, and the Nursing Strategic Vision.
Establishes structures for maintaining the  Healthy Work Environment standards of authentic leadership, skilled communication, true collaboration, meaningful recognition, appropriate staffing and effective decision making across the company.
Design and establish in collaboration with Human Resources a clinical ladder structure at Emplify that recognizes and rewards nurses for their education, professional development, and contributions to nursing at Emplify.
Leads collaborative work to develop innovative staffing models using knowledge of current nursing workforce trends that impact the number and availability of RNs in the workforce.
Partners with HR, Finance, and Regional nursing leaders to optimize Travel Nurse Agency contract agreements and prioritize appropriate and timely facility staffing.
Initiates and participates in problem-solving and policy creation and updates when needed.
Develops structures for standard nursing recognition elements across the enterprise.
Develops and supports plans for recruitment and retention of nurses to maintain an effective nursing workforce.
Provides oversight and direction for the design and structure of nursing leadership development initiatives across the enterprise.
Develops communication strategies for major initiatives and serve as a conduit of information and communication from the office of the CSO as applicable, to senior leaders, departments and, in conjunction with the Corporate Communications team, to the organization at-large.
Identifies and responds to issues and risks, own and provides expedient follow through to action or resolution as applicable, communicating accordingly and appropriately.
Functions as an “advisor” for health policy and national health system issues. Remain abreast of national trends in healthcare markets as the organization migrates towards a more consumer focused clinical company."', 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:24:02.2133333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:24:02.2133333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[essential_functions_original] ([id], [job_id], [function_text], [sort_order], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (247, 90, N'" Receive payments from third party payor lockbox and mail correspondence and post payments to patient claims in the patient accounting system
Review electronic remittances and resolve electronic posting exceptions and variances, posting payments to corresponding patient claims
Interpret Explanation of Benefits (EOBs) and transfer remaining patient and secondary insurance liability to the appropriate payor or next responsible party
