INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (14, 14, 1, N'The Plant Operator''s job is dealing boilers and compressor systems equipment in cooperation with all staff members in assisting with safe and effective patient care.  Also, the Plant Operator will ensure the safe and continuous operation of the Chiller and Cooling Towers if they are applicable to the facility. Performs any other duties as assigned and directed by the Facilities Supervisor in compliance with the philosophy, goals, policies and procedures of the facility.  The Plant Operator is responsible for adhering to the Corporate Compliance Plan, to the rules and regulations of all applicable local, state and federal agencies, and to the standards of all accrediting bodies.', N'Responsible for managing boilers and compressor systems equipment to support safe and effective patient care. This position ensures the safe and continuous operation of the Chiller and Cooling Towers if applicable to the facility. Additionally, this role performs any other duties as assigned and directed by the Facilities Supervisor. In addition, this position adheres to the Corporate Compliance Plan and complies with the rules and regulations of all applicable local, state, and federal agencies. Responsibilities for this role include maintaining standards set by accrediting bodies. Ensures all tasks are completed efficiently and to high standards.', N'Responsible for managing boilers and compressor systems equipment to support safe and effective patient care. This position ensures the safe and continuous operation of the Chiller and Cooling Towers if applicable to the facility. Additionally, this role performs any other duties as assigned and directed by the Facilities Supervisor. In addition, this position adheres to the Corporate Compliance Plan and complies with the rules and regulations of all applicable local, state, and federal agencies. Responsibilities for this role include maintaining standards set by accrediting bodies. Ensures all tasks are completed efficiently and to high standards.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Able to read blueprints
•  Must maintain current knowledge base of equipment and demonstrates thorough understanding of boiler systems
•  Able to communicate in English
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

