• 7+ work experience Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', N'great', 0, 11, CAST(N'2025-06-20T09:44:14.1466667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:31.5233333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:31.5233333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (16, 16, 1, N'The Cardiopulmonary Manager will deliver safe and effective care, which is consistent with the standards of care for this discipline. This role demands a deep understanding of the treatment of respiratory and cardiovascular disorders for both inpatients and outpatients, under the guidance of the Director and the Medical Director. The candidate must possess comprehensive knowledge of departmental and hospital policies and procedures as they pertain to Cardiopulmonary science. Operating independently within the critical care areas of the hospital is a key function of this position. Additionally, the Cardiopulmonary Manager will be expected to assume relief responsibilities in the Director''s absence, ensuring continuity of care and leadership. This position underscores the importance of expertise in Cardiopulmonary science and the ability to manage departmental functions effectively while aligning with established healthcare standards.', N'Responsible for delivering safe and effective care consistent with the standards of Cardiopulmonary science. This role demands a deep understanding of the treatment of respiratory and cardiovascular disorders for both inpatients and outpatients. Additionally, this position requires comprehensive knowledge of departmental and hospital policies and procedures. In addition, this role operates independently within the critical care areas of the hospital. Additionally, this position assumes relief responsibilities in the Director''s absence, ensuring continuity of care and leadership. This role underscores the importance of expertise in Cardiopulmonary science and the ability to manage departmental functions effectively while aligning with established healthcare standards.', N'Responsible for delivering safe and effective care consistent with the standards of Cardiopulmonary science. This role demands a deep understanding of the treatment of respiratory and cardiovascular disorders for both inpatients and outpatients. Additionally, this position requires comprehensive knowledge of departmental and hospital policies and procedures. In addition, this role operates independently within the critical care areas of the hospital. Additionally, this position assumes relief responsibilities in the Director''s absence, ensuring continuity of care and leadership. This role underscores the importance of expertise in Cardiopulmonary science and the ability to manage departmental functions effectively while aligning with established healthcare standards.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Must be a Registered Nurse, Registered Cardiac Sonographer, or Registered Respiratory Therapist.
•  Management skills and computer proficiency are required.

Education
• Associate Required

Field of Study
• in respiratory care

Experience
• hospital experience, and lead/supervisory experience for at least one year.

Licenses and Certifications
• Basic Life Support - CPR Cert (BLS) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:33.3700000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:33.3700000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:33.3700000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (17, 17, 1, N'Applies paints, stains, and other surface treatments to structural surfaces and property. Prepares surfaces by washing, scraping, sanding, torching and/or smoothing prior to applying finishing materials. Assists other trades as needed.', N'Responsible for applying paints, stains, and other surface treatments to structural surfaces and property. This position prepares surfaces by washing, scraping, sanding, torching, and smoothing prior to applying finishing materials. Additionally, this role ensures surfaces are properly treated to achieve desired finishes. In addition, this position assists other trades as needed to complete projects. Responsibilities for this role include maintaining tools and equipment, ensuring safety protocols are followed, and collaborating with team members. This role contributes to the overall maintenance and aesthetic quality of the organization''s facilities.', N'Responsible for applying paints, stains, and other surface treatments to structural surfaces and property. This position prepares surfaces by washing, scraping, sanding, torching, and smoothing prior to applying finishing materials. Additionally, this role ensures surfaces are properly treated to achieve desired finishes. In addition, this position assists other trades as needed to complete projects. Responsibilities for this role include maintaining tools and equipment, ensuring safety protocols are followed, and collaborating with team members. This role contributes to the overall maintenance and aesthetic quality of the organization''s facilities.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Knowledge of various paints, chemicals and combinations available for use Required
•  Able to communicate in English Required
•  Must have the ability to document records neatly and accurately Required
•  Ability to generate requisitions for materials and supplies Required
•  Ability to assign priority and teams in a timely manner Required
•  Ability to instruct others as per blueprints and work from sketches Required
•  Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or scheduled form Required
•  Ability to read, and interpret documents such as safety rules, operating and maintenance instructions, and procedure manuals Required
•  Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exist Required
•  Ability to calculate figures and amounts such as proportions, percentages, area, circumference, and volumes Required
•  Knowledge of safe handling tools and equipment Required
•  Basic Microsoft office computer skills Required
•  Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

