• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:39.2766667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:39.2766667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:39.2766667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (20, 20, 1, N'Biomedical Equipment Manager oversees the technicians in the overall operations of the Biomedical Department. Responsible for maintaining hospital compliance with regulatory agencies including DNV, AHCA, etc. Interacts and communicates appropriately with others to offer accurate and timely information and service in trouble-shooting and problem-solving capacity. Manages work and processes within span of control and regularly operates under deadlines and may be subject to extreme workloads. Performs planned maintenance and electrical safety inspections on a broad range of patient care and selected support equipment in compliance with established standards.', N'Responsible for overseeing the technicians in the overall operations of the Biomedical Department. This position maintains hospital compliance with regulatory agencies including DNV and AHCA. Additionally, this role interacts and communicates appropriately with others to offer accurate and timely information and service in troubleshooting and problem-solving capacity. In addition, this position manages work and processes within span of control and regularly operates under deadlines and may be subject to extreme workloads. Performs planned maintenance and electrical safety inspections on a broad range of patient care and selected support equipment in compliance with established standards.', N'Responsible for overseeing the technicians in the overall operations of the Biomedical Department. This position maintains hospital compliance with regulatory agencies including DNV and AHCA. Additionally, this role interacts and communicates appropriately with others to offer accurate and timely information and service in troubleshooting and problem-solving capacity. In addition, this position manages work and processes within span of control and regularly operates under deadlines and may be subject to extreme workloads. Performs planned maintenance and electrical safety inspections on a broad range of patient care and selected support equipment in compliance with established standards.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Ability to assemble, maintain, and repair various medical equipment Required
•  Knowledge of commonly-used concepts, practices, and procedures Required
•  Ability to maintain equipment and work areas in a clean and safe condition Required
•  Ability to logically read and comprehend technical manuals and instructions Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Required

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• in Marketing, or Communications

Experience
• 3+ years experience Required
•  5+ years of technical experience Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• Certified Biomedical Equipment Tech (CBET) Preferred

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:41.2333333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:41.2333333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:41.2333333' AS DateTime2))
