• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 11, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:43.2033333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:43.2033333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:43.2033333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (22, 22, 1, N'The chaplain is a member of the interdisciplinary healthcare team who provides for the spiritual needs of patients, their families, staff, and physicians.  Specifically, the chaplain, through professional training and certification, provides support and guidance to understand more fully life''s events as they relate to their spiritual and emotional well-being. Depending on the assessment of the clients served, their faith journey, culture and heritage, and life experience, the chaplain is effective through a variety of case specific interventions including but not limited to the following: listening, the ministry of presence, offering faith appropriate prayers, discussion and/or reflection. The chaplain is sensitive to all faiths, cultures, races, ages and creeds to assist in the mode most acceptable.  The Chaplain provides the spiritual support and encouragement so that the whole person may be served.

The Chaplain II PRN position is that of a Flex Chaplain with a flexible schedule to meet the patient care needs of the department and may include days, nights and/or weekend and on-call assignments with a minimum of one weekend per month, two nights per week.', N'Responsible for providing spiritual care to patients, their families, staff, and physicians as part of the interdisciplinary healthcare team. This position offers support and guidance through professional training and certification to help individuals understand life''s events in relation to their spiritual and emotional well-being. Additionally, this role utilizes various interventions such as listening, ministry of presence, faith-appropriate prayers, discussion, and reflection, tailored to the clients'' faith journey, culture, heritage, and life experience. In addition, this position is sensitive to all faiths, cultures, races, ages, and creeds to provide the most acceptable mode of spiritual support. Additionally, this role operates on a flexible schedule to meet patient care needs, including days, nights, weekends, and on-call assignments.', N'Responsible for providing spiritual care to patients, their families, staff, and physicians as part of the interdisciplinary healthcare team. This position offers support and guidance through professional training and certification to help individuals understand life''s events in relation to their spiritual and emotional well-being. Additionally, this role utilizes various interventions such as listening, ministry of presence, faith-appropriate prayers, discussion, and reflection, tailored to the clients'' faith journey, culture, heritage, and life experience. In addition, this position is sensitive to all faiths, cultures, races, ages, and creeds to provide the most acceptable mode of spiritual support. Additionally, this role operates on a flexible schedule to meet patient care needs, including days, nights, weekends, and on-call assignments.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Must be proficient in the English language. Required
•  Establish constructive working relationships with all members of the healthcare team, including staff chaplains, and community clergy and caregivers. Required
•  Full knowledge and understanding of whole person health principles and related spiritual needs Required
•  Proficient in spiritual care principles and assessment abilities Required
•  Meet computer requirements. Required
•  Able to enter Pastoral Care visit information in Cerner efficiently and correctly. Required
•  Knowledge to use effectively Microsoft Word and Outlook. Required
•  Must be willing to fill a flexible schedule for on-call and other assignments. Required
•  Debrief and crisis intervention Required
•  Personal commitment to God. Required
•  Enjoys collaboration and working as a team Required
•  Personal integrity and an ability to work under stress. Required
•  Ability to effectively relate to persons of diverse religious, educational, and cultural backgrounds. Required
•  Ability to earn respect of nurses, physicians, and other healthcare professionals. Required
•  Articulate an understanding of institutional culture, systems and corporate relationships
•  Preferred
•  Public speaking and communication skills for devotionals and other staff meetings
•  Preferred

Education
• Master''s Required

Field of Study
• of Divinity degree
•  2-4 units of Clinical Pastoral Education

Experience
• Previous experience as staff chaplain
•  Preferred
•  Education and/or experience in conflict resolution, public speaking, pastoral ministry or church elder
•  Preferred
•  Healthcare and Congregational pastoral experience 
•  
•  Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
•  Ordination Preferred

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:45.0500000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:45.0500000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:45.0500000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (23, 23, 1, N'Coordinate the work order request system, maintain logs and records for recurring inspections by outside agencies, use the Trane Tracer ES Building Automation System to adjust room temperatures and be a first responder for emergencies requiring the use of fire alarm panels, security lock system, medical gas alarm panels and order repair parts for the maintenance staff.', N'Responsible for coordinating the work order request system and maintaining logs and records for recurring inspections by outside agencies. This position uses the Trane Tracer ES Building Automation System to adjust room temperatures. Additionally, this role acts as a first responder for emergencies requiring the use of fire alarm panels, security lock systems, and medical gas alarm panels. In addition, this position orders repair parts for the maintenance staff. Responsibilities for this role include ensuring timely and accurate documentation of all maintenance activities. This role contributes to the overall operational efficiency and safety of the facility.', N'Responsible for coordinating the work order request system and maintaining logs and records for recurring inspections by outside agencies. This position uses the Trane Tracer ES Building Automation System to adjust room temperatures. Additionally, this role acts as a first responder for emergencies requiring the use of fire alarm panels, security lock systems, and medical gas alarm panels. In addition, this position orders repair parts for the maintenance staff. Responsibilities for this role include ensuring timely and accurate documentation of all maintenance activities. This role contributes to the overall operational efficiency and safety of the facility.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Ability to maintain meticulous record keeping of documents for inspections Required
•  Basic knowledge of electrical / mechanical systems nomenclatures to competently seek out replacement parts and order them for maintenance technicians Required
•  Excellent customer service skills to ensure customers are satisfied their maintenance requests are being attended to in a timely and efficient manner Required
•  Ability to master the operation of multiple complex electronic alarm panels and computerized systems such as Simplex Fire Alarm, Medical Gas, Generator, Fire Pump, Boilers, Fuel Oil Pump Required
•  Must be able to communicate in English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Experience using CMSS (Computerized Maintenance Management Software) such as PeopleSoft to manage the work order process Preferred
•  Knowledge of Joint Commission or DNV inspection requirements very desirable Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 2+ years of commercial building maintenance department employment or commercial construction work Required

Licenses and Certifications
• Driver''s License (DL) Preferred

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 11, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:46.9300000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:46.9300000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:46.9300000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (24, 24, 1, N'The Business Functions Coordinator position is responsible for the independent management, education, and operations of the department(s) in which he/she works.  The person in this role reports directly to their area director and must exercise discretion and judgment as it relates to all matters as most are confidential. Primary duties include but is not limited to independent work on: procurement of special (medical) items for their specific area(s); authority to formulate or interpret policies within their area in lieu of the director; obligating the department to pay for expenses; auditing, accounting, and management of time and attendance for their areas; ensuring staffing coverage; seeking out and working with outside companies; management of agency/travelers and other contractual service agreements; planning of events throughout the year, and in depth data analysis, reports and presentations; et cetera.', N'Responsible for the independent management, education, and operations of the department. This position manages procurement of special items, formulates or interprets policies, and obligates the department to pay for expenses. Additionally, this role audits, accounts, and manages time and attendance, ensuring staffing coverage. In addition, this position seeks out and collaborates with outside companies, manages agency/travelers and other contractual service agreements, and plans events throughout the year. Additionally, this role conducts in-depth data analysis, prepares reports, and delivers presentations. This position exercises discretion and judgment in all confidential matters.', N'Responsible for the independent management, education, and operations of the department. This position manages procurement of special items, formulates or interprets policies, and obligates the department to pay for expenses. Additionally, this role audits, accounts, and manages time and attendance, ensuring staffing coverage. In addition, this position seeks out and collaborates with outside companies, manages agency/travelers and other contractual service agreements, and plans events throughout the year. Additionally, this role conducts in-depth data analysis, prepares reports, and delivers presentations. This position exercises discretion and judgment in all confidential matters.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Must be fluent in the English language. Required
•  Proficient in Microsoft Word, Excel, Power Point, and other computer software required. Required
•  Excellent organizational skills. Required
•  Knowledge of medical terminology. Required
•  Knowledge in the use of current computer software applications, personal computers, and other office equipment. Required

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 1+ prior experience in a health care setting Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:49.5233333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:49.5233333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:21:49.5233333' AS DateTime2))
