s role monitors routine and preventative maintenance activities to ensure utilities, environmental systems, and other building systems operate properly and efficiently. In addition, this position works with Purchasing and other departments to manage equipment recall requests. Additionally, this role ensures compliance with policies and procedures to maintain operational efficiency.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Knowledge of ordering parts and supplies related to building maintenance and repairs Required
•  Ability to prioritize assignments Required
•  Working knowledge of regulatory requirements from DNV, TJC, AHCA, OSHA, NFPA and other health care related agencies Required
•  Working knowledge of all Facilities systems and equipment and all Biomedical systems and equipment. Required
•  Ability to read, comprehend, and interpret blue prints, diagrams/technical drawings, technical manuals and instructions, and Operation & Maintenance Manuals Required
•  Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Customer Relations Preferred
•  Interpersonal Skills Preferred
•  Knowledge of state and federal hazardous and biological waste regulations Preferred
•  Familiarity with building codes, NFPA, AHCA, The Joint Commission and or DNV standards Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• Grad or Equiv

Experience
• 4+ Required 

Licenses and Certifications
• Certified Biomedical Equipment Tech (CBET) or CHTM (Certified Healthcare Technology Manager) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• CHEPP (Certified Healthcare Emergency Power Professional)
• CHFM (Certified Healthcare Facility Management)  Required
• Stationary Power Engineer License very desirable (Steam low & high pressure)
• Universal Refrigeration EPA License', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:08.2500000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:08.2500000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:08.2500000' AS DateTime2))
