ient orders. This role supports pharmacists and provides distributive pharmacy services to ensure safe and accurate medication services, supporting all those involved in direct patient care.', N'Responsible for the provision of medication distributive functions and pharmacy operational tasks. This position assists the pharmacist with preparing and dispensing medications, inventory management, and regulatory compliance. In addition, this position performs duties necessary for the effective daily operation of all department services and programs. Additionally, this role accurately responds to medication dispensing requests, prepares medications for pharmacist final review, delivers checked medications, and returns unused or expired medications to appropriate pharmacy areas. Responsibilities for this role include preparing and organizing pharmacy medications by name and dosage as listed on patient orders. This role supports pharmacists and provides distributive pharmacy services to ensure safe and accurate medication services, supporting all those involved in direct patient care.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Strong verbal and written communication, organizational, problemsolving, and customer service skills Required
