• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:14.7066667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:14.7066667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:14.7066667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (38, 38, 1, N'Primary responsibility is the provision of medication distributive functions and pharmacy operational tasks, which includes but is not limited to assisting the pharmacist with all duties of preparing and dispensing of medications, inventory management, and regulatory compliance. Under the direct supervision of a pharmacist, performs duties necessary for the effective daily operation of all department services and programs, including the compounding, dispensing, charging, and delivery of medications to the patients. Accurately responds to medication dispensing requests, prepares medications for pharmacist final review/check, delivers checked medications, and returns unused or expired medications to appropriate pharmacy areas. Prepares sterile products such as IV solutions, piggyback containers, irrigations, TPNs, prefilled syringes, reconstituting of medications under aseptic conditions. Keeps work area and equipment clean and neat. Performs various clerical and specialized duties. Helps in the training of pharmacy technician I and newly hired pharmacy technicians. Accurately refills and conducts inventory of medication dispensing systems and accurately loads and unloads medications as directed. Assists in recording and distribution of large and small volume IV solutions. Performs all necessary tasks related to front reception area. Serves the needs of neonatal, pediatric, adult, adolescent, and geriatric patients. Provides distributive pharmacy services and technical support for the pharmacist, performing activities or tasks in specialty pharmacy services. Assists pharmacists in promoting an organized and functional pharmacy service, prepares medications for dispensing, and maintains records. Actively participates in outstanding customer service and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all.', N'Responsible for assisting the pharmacist with medication distributive functions and pharmacy operational tasks. This position performs duties necessary for the effective daily operation of all department services and programs, including compounding, dispensing, charging, and delivery of medications. In addition, this position accurately responds to medication dispensing requests, prepares medications for pharmacist final review, and returns unused or expired medications to appropriate pharmacy areas. Additionally, this role prepares sterile products under aseptic conditions and keeps the work area and equipment clean and neat. Responsibilities for this role include refilling and conducting inventory of medication dispensing systems, recording and distributing IV solutions, and performing tasks related to the front reception area. Provides distributive pharmacy services and technical support for the pharmacist, promoting an organized and functional pharmacy service.', N'Responsible for assisting the pharmacist with medication distributive functions and pharmacy operational tasks. This position performs duties necessary for the effective daily operation of all department services and programs, including compounding, dispensing, charging, and delivery of medications. In addition, this position accurately responds to medication dispensing requests, prepares medications for pharmacist final review, and returns unused or expired medications to appropriate pharmacy areas. Additionally, this role prepares sterile products under aseptic conditions and keeps the work area and equipment clean and neat. Responsibilities for this role include refilling and conducting inventory of medication dispensing systems, recording and distributing IV solutions, and performing tasks related to the front reception area. Provides distributive pharmacy services and technical support for the pharmacist, promoting an organized and functional pharmacy service.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Strong verbal and written communication, organizational, problem‐solving, and customer service skills Required
• Flexibility and willingness to adapt to changes as necessary Required
• Ability to interact constructively with supervisors, peers, and external customers Required
• Ability to follow direction from formal management personnel and work well under direct supervision of a pharmacist. Required
• Ability to identify, follow up, and resolve discrepancies Required
• Ability to identify, mitigate, and assist in resolving pharmacy operational or program issues Required
• Ability to keep accurate and complete records Required
• Knowledge of medical terminology Required
• Knowledge and competence in aseptic techniques Required
• Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Required
• Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
• Proficiency in hospital computer system technology and automation Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 1+ contemporary hospital pharmacy, retail or ambulatory Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• PHRMTECH-R - Registered Pharmacy Technician Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• Sterile Compounding Certification  Preferred or
• Current certification from Pharmacy Technician Certification Board (PTCB) or from the Institute for the Certification of Pharmacy Technicians (ICPT)  Preferred', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:19.2366667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:19.2366667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:19.2366667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (39, 39, 1, N'The Payroll Clerk ensures timely and accurate processing of assigned payroll transactions in accordance with published standards and controls. Answers requests and inquiries from the employees in the organization, taxing authorities, other third parties, and resolves issues accordingly while providing excellent customer service.', N'Responsible for ensuring timely and accurate processing of assigned payroll transactions in accordance with published standards and controls. This position answers requests and inquiries from employees, taxing authorities, and other third parties, resolving issues accordingly while providing excellent customer service. Additionally, this role maintains payroll records and ensures compliance with relevant regulations and policies. In addition, this position collaborates with other departments to address payroll-related concerns and improve processes. Additionally, this role supports the overall efficiency and accuracy of payroll operations.', N'Responsible for ensuring timely and accurate processing of assigned payroll transactions in accordance with published standards and controls. This position answers requests and inquiries from employees, taxing authorities, and other third parties, resolving issues accordingly while providing excellent customer service. Additionally, this role maintains payroll records and ensures compliance with relevant regulations and policies. In addition, this position collaborates with other departments to address payroll-related concerns and improve processes. Additionally, this role supports the overall efficiency and accuracy of payroll operations.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• 
• 
