Additional Licenses and Certifications
• An equivalent combination of education and relevant work experience may be considered in lieu of the stated degree requirement.', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:23.3233333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:23.3233333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:23.3233333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (40, 40, 1, N'The Pharmacy Technician Supervisor may have direct reports and holds primary responsibility for overseeing the pharmacy automation systems, technician scheduling, technician PDO/sick coverage, and technician assignments. This role is critical in ensuring the smooth operation of the pharmacy''s technical and logistical functions, including patient billing and inventory management activities. The supervisor is also tasked with preparing and organizing pharmacy medications by name and dosage as listed on patient orders and supports pharmacists in providing distributive pharmacy services. Additionally, they are responsible for supervising the daily activities of pharmacy technicians to ensure safe and accurate medication services and support all those involved in direct patient care. Facility-specific assignments may also encompass access to, but are not limited to, pharmacy charge data, CDM databases, wholesaler and purchase files, automated dispensing systems, pharmaceutical contracts, data files, as well as personnel and compensation data. This role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the pharmacy''s operations, ensuring compliance with regulations, and supporting the delivery of high-quality patient care.

Applicable State Pharmacy Technician Registration (RPT) - Required
Current certification from Nationally recognized Board/Association - Required
Sterile Compounding Certification, if applicable per state legislation -Preferred', N'Responsible for overseeing pharmacy automation systems, technician scheduling, PDO/sick coverage, and assignments. This position ensures the smooth operation of the pharmacy''s technical and logistical functions, including patient billing and inventory management. Additionally, this role prepares and organizes pharmacy medications by name and dosage as listed on patient orders and supports pharmacists in providing distributive pharmacy services. In addition, this position supervises the daily activities of pharmacy technicians to ensure safe and accurate medication services and supports all those involved in direct patient care. Facility-specific assignments may include access to pharmacy charge data, CDM databases, wholesaler and purchase files, automated dispensing systems, pharmaceutical contracts, data files, and personnel and compensation data. This role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the pharmacy''s operations, ensuring compliance with regulations, and supporting the delivery of high-quality patient care.', N'Responsible for overseeing pharmacy automation systems, technician scheduling, PDO/sick coverage, and assignments. This position ensures the smooth operation of the pharmacy''s technical and logistical functions, including patient billing and inventory management. Additionally, this role prepares and organizes pharmacy medications by name and dosage as listed on patient orders and supports pharmacists in providing distributive pharmacy services. In addition, this position supervises the daily activities of pharmacy technicians to ensure safe and accurate medication services and supports all those involved in direct patient care. Facility-specific assignments may include access to pharmacy charge data, CDM databases, wholesaler and purchase files, automated dispensing systems, pharmaceutical contracts, data files, and personnel and compensation data. This role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the pharmacy''s operations, ensuring compliance with regulations, and supporting the delivery of high-quality patient care.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• •	Strong verbal and written communication, organizational, problem‐solving, and customer service skills
• •	Flexibility and willingness to adapt to changes as necessary
• •	Ability to interact constructively with supervisors, peers, and external customers
• •	Ability to follow direction from formal management personnel and informal supervisors (pharmacists) and at times, to work well without direct supervision
• •	Ability to identify, follow up, and resolve discrepancies
• •	Ability to identify, resolve, and mitigate pharmacy operational or program issues
• •	Ability to keep accurate and complete records
• •	Knowledge of medical terminology
• •	Ability to teach pharmacy technician students, if applicable
• •	Proficiency in hospital computer system technology and automation
• •	Knowledge and competence in aseptic techniques chemotherapy product compounding (if applicable)
• •	Initiative to keep abreast of and communicate developments in the provision of pharmacy services
• •	Ability to coordinate and lead small groups of people in determining in the provision of pharmacy services 
• •	Leader qualities essential to operate effectively within the institution and advance the practice of pharmacy 
• •	Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English
• •	Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office
• •	Performs other duties as assigned Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 3+ Of Contemporary hospital pharmacy experience Required

Licenses and Certifications
• PHRMTECH-R - Registered Pharmacy Technician Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• Applicable State Pharmacy Technician Registration (RPT) - Required  Required
• Current certification from Nationally recognized Board/Association - Required  Required
• Sterile Compounding Certification, if applicable per state legislation - Preferred  Preferred', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:25.1533333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:25.1533333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:25.1533333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (41, 41, 1, N'The Laboratory Assistant I performs various laboratory support procedures in assigned areas which may include phlebotomy and/or specimen processing in clinical and anatomical pathology areas.  The Laboratory Assistant I must meet the required basic continuing education and department specific requirements. Work customarily involves practical knowledge in various laboratory procedures and support functions. May be asked to perform any of the following non-technical functions:', N'Responsible for performing various laboratory support procedures in assigned areas, including phlebotomy and specimen processing in clinical and anatomical pathology areas. This position meets the required basic continuing education and department-specific requirements. In addition, this position involves practical knowledge in various laboratory procedures and support functions. Additionally, this role may be asked to perform non-technical functions. Responsibilities for this role include equipment maintenance, function checks, inventory control, blood specimen collection, and biological specimen processing. This position ensures adherence to safety policies and confidentiality regulations.', N'Responsible for performing various laboratory support procedures in assigned areas, including phlebotomy and specimen processing in clinical and anatomical pathology areas. This position meets the required basic continuing education and department-specific requirements. In addition, this position involves practical knowledge in various laboratory procedures and support functions. Additionally, this role may be asked to perform non-technical functions. Responsibilities for this role include equipment maintenance, function checks, inventory control, blood specimen collection, and biological specimen processing. This position ensures adherence to safety policies and confidentiality regulations.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Technical skills and aptitudes related to the laboratory procedures or processes performed in department or work area assigned.
•  Able to effectively communicate verbally and in written form in English with patients, staff, and customers of varied backgrounds in a respectful, effective, and professional manner.
•  Ability to read text and numbers in English, with demonstrated ability to comprehend, measure, reason, match, problem solve, and exercise judgment under supervision.
•  Ability to learn and apply computer related applications and programs, including using electronic keyboards and other peripheral devices.
•  Mature judgment and the ability to handle confidential information within guidelines and applicable regulations.
•  Ability to handle infectious biological specimens, caustics, toxic chemicals and/or irritants appropriately and safely.
•  Must be able to read, write, speak, and have good comprehension of conversational English.
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office.
•  Performs waived testing with uniformity, consistency, reliability, reproducibility, quality, and integrity of results, if applicable.
•  Phlebotomy skills.
•  Excellent customer service skills.

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• phlebotomy training program

Experience
• Six Months in Emplify Lab Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• Driver''s License (DL) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• Must meet one of either preferred Work Experience or Education is required', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:27.6033333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:27.6033333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:27.6033333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (42, 42, 1, N'Provides direct behavioral health patient care.', N'Responsible for providing direct behavioral health patient care. This position assesses patient needs and develops appropriate care plans. Additionally, this role implements therapeutic interventions to support patient recovery. In addition, this position monitors patient progress and adjusts treatment plans as necessary. Additionally, this role collaborates with healthcare professionals to ensure comprehensive care. Ensures the effective delivery of behavioral health services to improve patient outcomes.', N'Responsible for providing direct behavioral health patient care. This position assesses patient needs and develops appropriate care plans. Additionally, this role implements therapeutic interventions to support patient recovery. In addition, this position monitors patient progress and adjusts treatment plans as necessary. Additionally, this role collaborates with healthcare professionals to ensure comprehensive care. Ensures the effective delivery of behavioral health services to improve patient outcomes.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Ability to communicate appropriately, professionally, and effectively with patients and their family, hospital staff, nurses, physicians, and other health care professionals Required
•  Knowledge of commonly used concepts, practices, and procedures in the health care industry Required
•  Up-to-date knowledge of regulatory requirements and local, state, and national laws Required
•  Ability to understand and process instructions from physicians and other personnel Required
•  Proficiency in computer systems to enter and track patient records Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Must be able to read, write, and speak conversational English Required
•  Customer service skills Required
•  Organizational ability, sound judgment, and initiative Required
•  Knowledge of substance use disorder and behavioral health terminology with various treatment approaches Required
•  Adequate knowledge of activities of daily living Required
•  Ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing Required
•  Additional languages Preferred
•  Understanding and the ability to lead group activities Required
•  Knowledge of electronic medical records Preferred
•  Strong competence in Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint, and Word Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• in a Social Science

Experience
• medical office experience

Licenses and Certifications
• Basic Life Support - CPR Cert (BLS) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:29.6300000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:29.6300000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:29.6300000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (43, 43, 1, N'The Clinical Pharmacy Manager shall support the mission of the department, hospital, and health-system by preventing, identifying, and resolving drug-related problems to assure patient safety, improve patient satisfaction, optimize patient outcome, and minimize cost. They perform all functions of a registered pharmacist including accurate and timely dispensing, clinical interaction with the healthcare team, patient teaching, pharmacist and technician supervision. Additionally, this role encompasses the front-line management of clinical practice and direct leadership of Pharmacy Clinical Divisions, including decentralized pharmacy practice, medication use systems, and patient-centered pharmacy services. Responsibilities also involve managing the integration of clinical pharmacy services, drug utilization programs, and pharmacy operations, ensuring medication use aligns with evidence-based best practices and regulatory standards. This includes managing medication safety systems, regulatory compliance initiatives, patient quality services, and disease outcomes programs. The Clinical Pharmacy Manager actively functions as a member of clinical practice and interdisciplinary teams, delivering direct patient care, integrated operational services, pharmacist interventions, and medication therapy management across a broad range of disease states. This position directs the activities of pharmacists in assigned areas, oversees day-to-day staffing, and ensures effective provision of pharmacy services and medication therapy. The role includes educating staff, developing and enforcing institutional policies, managing human, capital, and operational resources, and actively participating in customer service while maintaining respectful relationships with all.

Applicable Pharmacy License - Required
Board of Pharmaceutical Specialties certification - Preferred', N'Responsible for preventing, identifying, and resolving drug-related problems to ensure patient safety, improve patient satisfaction, optimize patient outcomes, and minimize costs. This position performs all functions of a registered pharmacist, including accurate and timely dispensing, clinical interaction with the healthcare team, patient teaching, and supervision of pharmacists and technicians. Additionally, this role manages clinical practice and leads Pharmacy Clinical Divisions, including decentralized pharmacy practice, medication use systems, and patient-centered pharmacy services. In addition, this position integrates clinical pharmacy services, drug utilization programs, and pharmacy operations, ensuring medication use aligns with evidence-based best practices and regulatory standards. Additionally, this role manages medication safety systems, regulatory compliance initiatives, patient quality services, and disease outcomes programs. Responsible for educating staff, developing and enforcing institutional policies, managing resources, and participating in customer service while maintaining respectful relationships.', N'Responsible for preventing, identifying, and resolving drug-related problems to ensure patient safety, improve patient satisfaction, optimize patient outcomes, and minimize costs. This position performs all functions of a registered pharmacist, including accurate and timely dispensing, clinical interaction with the healthcare team, patient teaching, and supervision of pharmacists and technicians. Additionally, this role manages clinical practice and leads Pharmacy Clinical Divisions, including decentralized pharmacy practice, medication use systems, and patient-centered pharmacy services. In addition, this position integrates clinical pharmacy services, drug utilization programs, and pharmacy operations, ensuring medication use aligns with evidence-based best practices and regulatory standards. Additionally, this role manages medication safety systems, regulatory compliance initiatives, patient quality services, and disease outcomes programs. Responsible for educating staff, developing and enforcing institutional policies, managing resources, and participating in customer service while maintaining respectful relationships.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• •Strong verbal and written communication, organizational, problem‐solving, and customer service skills
• •Flexibility and willingness to adapt to changes as necessary
• •Works under minimal supervision, while using independent judgement
• •Ability to interact constructively with supervisors, peers, and support personnel
• •Ability to analyze data and follow up and resolve discrepancies
• •Ability to keep accurate and complete records
• •Ability to teach, precept, or facilitate training
• •Initiative to keep abreast of new information/products/developments in the field of pharmacy
• •Working knowledge of the American Society of Health-System Pharmacists Accreditation Standards for Pharmacy 
• Residency Programs, if applicable
• •Ability to coordinate and lead small groups of people in determining policy, implementing procedures and 
• demonstrating progress
• •Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English
• •Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office
• •Performs other duties as assigned Required

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 3+ Related experience Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• BCLS - Basic Life Support - if applicable to facility Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:31.3533333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:31.3533333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:31.3533333' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (44, 44, 1, N'Under direct supervision, this position provides clerical office/departmental support. Responsibilities may include answering incoming calls, routing calls to appropriate location, greeting and directing visitors, mail distribution, ordering of supplies, office/department scheduling, and all other clerical related duties.', N'Responsible for providing clerical office and departmental support. This position answers incoming calls and routes them to the appropriate location. Additionally, this role greets and directs visitors, ensuring they reach their intended destinations. In addition, this position handles mail distribution and orders supplies as needed. Responsibilities for this role include office and departmental scheduling, along with other clerical duties. This role contributes to the smooth operation of the office and department through efficient and organized support.', N'Responsible for providing clerical office and departmental support. This position answers incoming calls and routes them to the appropriate location. Additionally, this role greets and directs visitors, ensuring they reach their intended destinations. In addition, this position handles mail distribution and orders supplies as needed. Responsibilities for this role include office and departmental scheduling, along with other clerical duties. This role contributes to the smooth operation of the office and department through efficient and organized support.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Knowledge of basic math and modern office equipment (fax machine, copy machine, scanner, etc.) Required
•  Proficient in Microsoft Office, including Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint, and Word Required
•  Basic and intermediate computer knowledge and skills Required
•  Able to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing Required
•  Additional languages Preferred
•  Effective time management and organizational skills Required
•  Ability to display professional interactions with all levels of internal and external customers Required
•  Excellent communication skills Required
•  Knowledge of medical terminology and the home health referral process Required
•  High level of multitasking, organization, and proactive communication skills Required
•  Ability to adapt to new situations and responsibilities Preferred
•  Effectively able to problem solve in complex situations Preferred
•  Excellent written communication skills Preferred
•  A notary public Preferred
•  Experience with constituent relationship management software such as Raisers Edge, Salesforce, etc. Required
•  Ability to work independently in a deadline-oriented team environment Required

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• in nutrition

Experience
• 1+ Medical Office Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:32.3700000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:32.3700000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:32.3700000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (45, 45, 1, N'The Social Media Communications Manager is responsible for creating and managing the social media platforms that elevate global strategic initiatives. The position actively collaborates with the marketing, communications and senior leadership teams to curate content and advise on future social media strategies and opportunities. The Social Media Communications Manager collaborates with the communications and marketing team to create an editorial calendar and structure that aligns content with volume driving marketing campaigns, brand messaging and internal and external communication strategies. Develops social media strategies with core internal audiences to help elevate team culture and morale while promoting messaging on the service standards, mission, vision and values inside Emplify. The Social Media Communications Manager also works directly with regional and corporate teams to develop and manage best practices for digital execution, monitoring and successful engagement results on social media platforms. Position reports to the Director of Corporate Communications.', N'Responsible for creating and managing social media platforms to elevate global strategic initiatives. This position collaborates with marketing, communications, and senior leadership teams to curate content and advise on future social media strategies. Additionally, this role creates an editorial calendar that aligns content with marketing campaigns, brand messaging, and communication strategies. In addition, this position develops social media strategies with internal audiences to enhance team culture and morale. Ensures best practices for digital execution, monitoring, and engagement results on social media platforms.', N'Responsible for creating and managing social media platforms to elevate global strategic initiatives. This position collaborates with marketing, communications, and senior leadership teams to curate content and advise on future social media strategies. Additionally, this role creates an editorial calendar that aligns content with marketing campaigns, brand messaging, and communication strategies. In addition, this position develops social media strategies with internal audiences to enhance team culture and morale. Ensures best practices for digital execution, monitoring, and engagement results on social media platforms.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Proficient in back end website and social media platforms and software systems to effectively execute and maintain public facing pages on various social media sites. Preferred
•  Proficient in the use of various social media platforms including but not limited to, Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, LinkedIn, Pinterest and YouTube. Preferred
•  Ability to use video, photo and edit capabilities from a smartphone to produce content for social media platforms. Preferred
•  Demonstrates leadership and management skills that unites the team and builds positive working relationships across departments. Preferred
•  Demonstrates strong professional interpersonal skills and ability to interact with all levels of management (internal and external), as well as media partners, vendors, community partners and the general public. Preferred
•  Ability to bridge the gap between executive leadership and front-line staff, creating action plans and messaging covering a multitude of campus and system goals shared across a variety of internal vehicles. Preferred
•  Proficient with Microsoft Office programs to include: PowerPoint, Excel, Word and Outlook. Preferred
•  Must have strong organizational skills, strong attention to detail and ability and willingness to multi-task and manage multiple projects in a fast-paced environment. Preferred
•  Strong time management and project management skills with ability to finish projects on deadline. Preferred
•  Assist in development and implement crisis communication plans as it relates to social media. Preferred
•  Must possess strong written communication skills that effectively use brand messaging and best practices set forth by Emplify to create robust engagement on social media. Preferred
•  Ability to work independently without supervision. Must be responsible and proactive with the ability to complete assignments in the absence of the Director. Ability to effectively solve problems and manage conflict. Preferred
•  Ability to manage information that may be confidential in nature. Preferred
•  Must be a team player. Preferred
•  Must display a professional manor at all times and be hard working and ethical. Preferred
•  Social media deployment and engagement. Preferred
•  Social media management in a corporate and/or multi location organizational structure. Preferred
•  Social media video, photo and editing on DSLR, cell phone or desktop computer. Preferred

Education
• Associate Required

