INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (50, 50, 1, N'The PBX Communications Specialist is responsible for operating the Facility switchboard consoles and for circulating applicable communications via mass paging systems for the region – in a high call volume setting. Performs most hospital overhead paging, monitors and responds promptly to all codes and alerts, fire alarms, tests and drills, and emergency situations-using proper procedure, and promptly answers and forwards all phone calls, internally and externally, to the proper extensions or persons. Responsible for communication of critical emergency response teams, as required. Responsible for facilitating paging of chaplains and various on-call teams for various areas. Provides directory assistance services for staff, patients, families and physicians, as requested. Records daily events on various report logs. Facilitates and screens international call requests. Effectively demonstrates the mission, vision, and values of Emplify throughout each and every interaction.', N'Responsible for operating the Facility switchboard consoles and circulating applicable communications via mass paging systems for the region. This position performs most hospital overhead paging, monitors and responds promptly to all codes and alerts, fire alarms, tests and drills, and emergency situations using proper procedure. Additionally, this role promptly answers and forwards all phone calls, internally and externally, to the proper extensions or persons. In addition, this position communicates with critical emergency response teams as required and facilitates paging of chaplains and various on-call teams for various areas. Responsibilities for this role include providing directory assistance services for staff, patients, families, and physicians, recording daily events on various report logs, and facilitating and screening international call requests. This role effectively demonstrates the mission, vision, and values of the organization throughout each interaction.', N'Responsible for operating the Facility switchboard consoles and circulating applicable communications via mass paging systems for the region. This position performs most hospital overhead paging, monitors and responds promptly to all codes and alerts, fire alarms, tests and drills, and emergency situations using proper procedure. Additionally, this role promptly answers and forwards all phone calls, internally and externally, to the proper extensions or persons. In addition, this position communicates with critical emergency response teams as required and facilitates paging of chaplains and various on-call teams for various areas. Responsibilities for this role include providing directory assistance services for staff, patients, families, and physicians, recording daily events on various report logs, and facilitating and screening international call requests. This role effectively demonstrates the mission, vision, and values of the organization throughout each interaction.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Ability to remain calm, composed, and professional at all times Required
•  Demonstrates effective communication with all team members, callers, staff, patients, and families. Ability to speak with callers distinctly and clearly Required
•  Ability to remain attentive for incoming codes and alerts Required
•  Ability and willingness to quickly adapt to change Required
•  Demonstrates a sense of urgency in emergency matters. Able to readapt swiftly, as required Required
•  Ability to think proactively, progressively, compassionately, and responsibly Required
•  Ability to follow instructions and timely respond to all matters during normal or stressful conditions alike Required
•  Ability to multi-task (i.e., read and respond to emails, document events, take calls, and communicate with team, as needed) Required
•  Ability and willingness to work in a team environment as well as independently Required
•  Ability to remain engaged while also maintaining satisfactory participation and attendance for all meetings and staff development programs Required
•  Ability to work a variable/flexible shift to include nights, weekends, and holidays Required
•  Complies with the Facility Employee Code of Conduct Required
•  Demonstrates compliance with all HIPAA, federal, state, and local laws, rules, and government Required
•  Promotes evidence of adherence to the hospital confidentiality policy Required
•  High school graduate or equivalent. Required
•  One (1) year PBX switchboard/operator, call center  high call volume environment, clerical/administrative, hospitality, and/or customer service-focused experience Required
•  Excellent customer service Preferred
•  Ability to comprehensively document event details accurately Preferred
•  Proficiency in reading, writing/spelling, and communicating information. (English) Preferred
•  Willingness to learn and advance in role Preferred
•  Ability to follow instruction Preferred
•  Ability to respond to urgent matters accordingly Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• years experience
•  year PBX switchboard/operator, call center  high call volume environment, clerical/administrative, hospitality, and/or customer service-focused experience
•  years PBX switchboard/operator, call center  high call volume environment, clerical/administrative, hospitality, and/or customer service-focused experience
•  year experience in a hospital and/or a medical / healthcare setting

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:44.4666667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:44.4666667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:44.4666667' AS DateTime2))
