Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:46.5866667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:46.5866667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:46.5866667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (52, 52, 1, N'This position will have responsibility for managing and maintaining supply stock in a specialty department or procedure area and building relationships with staff members in the department. The Specialty Supply Chain Coordinator will be responsible for supplier relationships, requisitioning supplies, equipment, and services, and processing bill-only and consignment requisitions. This position will be responsible for managing inventory levels, ensuring new products are properly reviewed prior to purchasing, keeping supply areas clean and neat, managing consignments and expiring goods, processing returns, updating shelf labels, and completing all computer software functions necessary to ensure that the appropriate supplies and equipment are available and accurate transactions are recorded.', N'Responsible for managing and maintaining supply stock in a specialty department or procedure area. This position oversees supplier relationships, requisitions supplies, equipment, and services, and processes bill-only and consignment requisitions. Additionally, this role manages inventory levels, ensures new products are properly reviewed prior to purchasing, keeps supply areas clean and neat, manages consignments and expiring goods, processes returns, updates shelf labels, and completes all necessary computer software functions. In addition, this position builds relationships with staff members in the department to ensure efficient operations. Ensures that appropriate supplies and equipment are available and accurate transactions are recorded.', N'Responsible for managing and maintaining supply stock in a specialty department or procedure area. This position oversees supplier relationships, requisitions supplies, equipment, and services, and processes bill-only and consignment requisitions. Additionally, this role manages inventory levels, ensures new products are properly reviewed prior to purchasing, keeps supply areas clean and neat, manages consignments and expiring goods, processes returns, updates shelf labels, and completes all necessary computer software functions. In addition, this position builds relationships with staff members in the department to ensure efficient operations. Ensures that appropriate supplies and equipment are available and accurate transactions are recorded.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Basic knowledge of products and equipment used in the specialty area. Required
•  Proficient in use of Microsoft Outlook, Word, and Excel. Required
•  Demonstrated ability to work independently. Required
•  Able to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. Required
•  Understanding of clinical procedure processes. Required
•  In-depth knowledge of products and equipment used in specialty area. Preferred
•  Some knowledge and experience in performing the duties associated with purchasing, receiving, shipping, and distribution. Preferred
•  Demonstrates ability to use an ERP system. Preferred

Education
• Associate Required

Field of Study
• or 5 years

Experience
• 6 -12 months healthcare  experience Required 
• 6 months Peoplesoft experience Preferred 

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:48.4000000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:48.4000000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:48.4000000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (53, 53, 1, N'Primary responsibility is the provision of integrated clinical and distributive pharmacy services, decentralized inter-professional pharmacy practice, direct patient care programs, expert experiential pharmacy student and pharmacy resident training, and leadership of quality improvement and practice advancement initiatives.  Proficiently leads general and specialty direct patient care programs, advanced drug management services, and medication use systems throughout the institution.  Actively functions as a member of clinical pharmacy services, decentralized pharmacy practice programs, and multidisciplinary teams to proficiently complete critical medication order scrutiny, drug profile review, and monitoring of patients with a broad range of disease states to identify, prevent, or mitigate medication-related problems.  Actively participates in medication safety systems, regulatory compliance initiatives, patient quality services, and disease outcomes programs.  Delivers general and specialty medication therapy management consult services and disease state management services as needed and proactively intervenes in all areas of medication use as appropriate to optimize patient outcomes.  Actively participates in outstanding customer service and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all.', N'Responsible for providing integrated clinical and distributive pharmacy services, decentralized inter-professional pharmacy practice, direct patient care programs, and leadership of quality improvement initiatives. This position leads general and specialty direct patient care programs, advanced drug management services, and medication use systems throughout the institution. Additionally, this role functions as a member of clinical pharmacy services, decentralized pharmacy practice programs, and multidisciplinary teams to complete critical medication order scrutiny, drug profile review, and patient monitoring. In addition, this position participates in medication safety systems, regulatory compliance initiatives, patient quality services, and disease outcomes programs. Additionally, this role delivers general and specialty medication therapy management consult services and disease state management services, proactively intervening in all areas of medication use to optimize patient outcomes. This position actively participates in outstanding customer service and maintains respectful relationships with all.', N'Responsible for providing integrated clinical and distributive pharmacy services, decentralized inter-professional pharmacy practice, direct patient care programs, and leadership of quality improvement initiatives. This position leads general and specialty direct patient care programs, advanced drug management services, and medication use systems throughout the institution. Additionally, this role functions as a member of clinical pharmacy services, decentralized pharmacy practice programs, and multidisciplinary teams to complete critical medication order scrutiny, drug profile review, and patient monitoring. In addition, this position participates in medication safety systems, regulatory compliance initiatives, patient quality services, and disease outcomes programs. Additionally, this role delivers general and specialty medication therapy management consult services and disease state management services, proactively intervening in all areas of medication use to optimize patient outcomes. This position actively participates in outstanding customer service and maintains respectful relationships with all.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Strong verbal and written communication, organizational, problem-solving, and customer service skills Required
•  Flexibility and willingness to adapt to changes as necessary Required
•  Ability to work well without supervision and to supervise personnel Required
•  Ability to interact constructively with supervisors, peers, and support personnel Required
•  Ability to analyze data and follow up and resolve discrepancies Required
•  Ability to keep accurate and complete records Required
•  Ability to teach, precept, and facilitate experiential training Required
•  Initiative to keep abreast of developments in the provision of pharmacy services Required
•  Initiative to keep abreast of new information/products/developments in the field of pharmacy Required
•  Proficiency in general hospital pharmacy operations and regulatory compliance Required
•  Proficiency with hospital computer systems, pharmacy technology, and pharmacy automation Required
•  Proficiency in hospital pharmacy practice, patient-centered care, advanced pharmacy practice, medication therapy management, and evidence-based medicine Required
•  Working knowledge of the American Society of Health-System Pharmacists Accreditation Standards for Pharmacy Residency Programs Required
•  Ability to coordinate and lead small groups of people in determining policy, implementing procedures and demonstrating progress Required
•  Leadership qualities essential to operate effectively within the institution and advance the practice of pharmacy Required
•  Must be able to read, write, speak, and have good comprehension of conversational English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Ability to define operational or program problems/needs and solutions Preferred
•  Ability to integrate clinical and distributive pharmacy services with quality improvement, teaching, research, and professional development activities Preferred
•  Expertise using Cerner pharmacy solutions and services Preferred
•  Expertise using Pyxis automated dispensing technology Preferred
•  Working analytical and data management skills Preferred
•  Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint Preferred
•  Working knowledge of the accreditation requirements of Det Norske Veritas and International Organization for Standardization quality management systems Preferred
•  Working knowledge of the American Society of Health-System Pharmacists National Practice Standards Preferred

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• of Science in Pharmacy OR Doctor of Pharmacy
•  Post Graduate Year One (PGY1) AND Post Graduate Year Two (PGY2) Pharmacy Residency in specialty area consistent with practice needs of institution
•  PGY1 Residency plus contemporary hospital or specialty practice experience (3+ years) consistent with practice needs of institution

Experience
• 5+ Clinical pharmacy experience in contemporary hospital or specialty practice (5+ years) consistent with practice needs of institution Required
•  Practice experience in a large hospital (greater than 500 bed institution) and integrated healthcare system (three or more hospitals in system) Preferred
•  Pharmacy leadership experience within a hospital setting or professional organization Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• Licensed Pharmacist (RPH) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:50.1900000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:50.1900000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:50.1900000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (54, 54, 1, N'The Senior Executive Assistant position is responsible for fully supporting assigned Senior Executive Vice President(s) within the department. This position is responsible for complete management of the Executive''s calendars, including but not limited to scheduling appointments, coordinating all arrangements for meetings, conferences, and travel. Prepares routine and non-routine reports and presentations, including gathering and summarizing data. Establishes and maintains highly confidential files and records. Composes letters and correspondence. Answers phones, delivers outstanding customer service, and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all. May provide project management, assistance with budget planning and tracking, statistical reporting, or other data tasks as required by the department.', N'Responsible for fully supporting assigned Senior Executive Vice President(s) within the department. This position manages the Executive''s calendars, including scheduling appointments, coordinating arrangements for meetings, conferences, and travel. Additionally, this role prepares routine and non-routine reports and presentations, gathering and summarizing data. In addition, this position establishes and maintains highly confidential files and records, and composes letters and correspondence. Additionally, this role answers phones, delivers outstanding customer service, and maintains respectful relationships. May provide project management, assistance with budget planning and tracking, statistical reporting, or other data tasks as required by the department.', N'Responsible for fully supporting assigned Senior Executive Vice President(s) within the department. This position manages the Executive''s calendars, including scheduling appointments, coordinating arrangements for meetings, conferences, and travel. Additionally, this role prepares routine and non-routine reports and presentations, gathering and summarizing data. In addition, this position establishes and maintains highly confidential files and records, and composes letters and correspondence. Additionally, this role answers phones, delivers outstanding customer service, and maintains respectful relationships. May provide project management, assistance with budget planning and tracking, statistical reporting, or other data tasks as required by the department.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Proficient in Microsoft Office, including Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint, and Word Required
•  Strong emphasis on organizational skills and strong attention to detail Required
•  Ability and willingness to multitask Required
•  Ability to display professional interactions with all levels of internal and external customers Required
•  Must be able to read, write, and speak conversational English Required
•  Excellent verbal and written communication skills Required
•  Ability to deal with data that is of a sensitive and confidential nature Required
•  Ability to work independently or in a team environment Required
•  Able to take initiative to solve issues and proactively prepare for upcoming events Required
•  Effectively able to problem-solve in complex situations Required
•  Ability to adapt to new situations and responsibilities Required
•  Analytical skills Required
•  Time management and planning skills Required
•  A notary public Preferred

Education
• Associate Preferred

Field of Study
• Culinary Arts certification or degree in hospitality

Experience
• 5+ experience Required

Licenses and Certifications
• National Notary Association Notary Public (NNANP) Preferred

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• Culinary Arts certification Preferred', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:52.7000000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:52.7000000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:22:52.7000000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (55, 55, 1, N'Installs, operates and maintains the organization''s heating and air conditioning (HVAC) systems.', N'Responsible for installing, operating, and maintaining the organization''s heating and air conditioning (HVAC) systems. This position ensures the efficient functioning of HVAC systems to provide a comfortable environment. Additionally, this role performs regular inspections and preventive maintenance to avoid system failures. In addition, this position troubleshoots and repairs HVAC equipment as needed. Additionally, this role collaborates with other departments to address HVAC-related issues promptly. Ensures compliance with safety standards and regulations in all HVAC operations.', N'Responsible for installing, operating, and maintaining the organization''s heating and air conditioning (HVAC) systems. This position ensures the efficient functioning of HVAC systems to provide a comfortable environment. Additionally, this role performs regular inspections and preventive maintenance to avoid system failures. In addition, this position troubleshoots and repairs HVAC equipment as needed. Additionally, this role collaborates with other departments to address HVAC-related issues promptly. Ensures compliance with safety standards and regulations in all HVAC operations.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Ability to identify equipment needs, parts and supplies, and maintain adequate inventory Required
