INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (60, 60, 1, N'The Supply Chain Supervisor is responsible for managing assigned components of daily supply chain operations at the facility, including the warehouse where applicable. The Supervisor will oversee assigned staff members'' daily performance and may serve as their direct report. This position will build and maintain relationships with key hospital stakeholders to ensure supply chain is meeting and exceeding customer needs. The Supply Chain Supervisor is ultimately responsible for ensuring the operational effectiveness of their assigned area and team.', N'Responsible for managing assigned components of daily supply chain operations at the facility, including the warehouse where applicable. This position oversees the daily performance of assigned staff members and may serve as their direct report. Additionally, this role builds and maintains relationships with key hospital stakeholders to ensure the supply chain meets and exceeds customer needs. In addition, this position ensures the operational effectiveness of the assigned area and team. Additionally, this role implements internal controls and reporting to ensure compliance with policies, procedures, processes, and contracts.', N'Responsible for managing assigned components of daily supply chain operations at the facility, including the warehouse where applicable. This position oversees the daily performance of assigned staff members and may serve as their direct report. Additionally, this role builds and maintains relationships with key hospital stakeholders to ensure the supply chain meets and exceeds customer needs. In addition, this position ensures the operational effectiveness of the assigned area and team. Additionally, this role implements internal controls and reporting to ensure compliance with policies, procedures, processes, and contracts.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Strong computer skills, including Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook Required
•  Analytical skills Required
•  Ability to coordinate and schedule activities of staff members Required
•  Ability to manage multiple projects with competing priorities Required
•  Strong customer service, communication, and persuasive presentation skills Required
•  ERP Preferred

Education
• Associate Preferred

Field of Study
• in Exercise Science or a related field, such as, Kinesiology, Kinesiotherapy, Athletic Training, Physiology, Sports Management, Exercise Physiology, Human Performance, Health Science, or Recreation Management/Science

Experience
• 3+ experience Preferred
•  Supervisory experience Preferred
•  6 months Peoplesoft experience Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:04.2700000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:04.2700000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:04.2700000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (61, 61, 1, N'The Lead Paramedic is a Paramedic that assists with management of shift operations to ensure efficient movement of all requests for Emplify patient transports. The Lead Paramedic functions as one member of a crew assigned to an Emplify ambulance and will transport patients when necessary.  The Lead Paramedic is also responsible for (under the direction of the Supervisor and in cooperation with the Supervisor) rounding with on duty crews at outlying campuses and HBEDs, delivering supplies as necessary, assisting other crews with lifting and/or transporting patients, rounding with the staff at outlying Emergency Departments. The Lead Paramedic may also inspect the Emplify ambulances that are in service for cleanliness and preparedness. Meets department metrics and standards of care, adheres to the Emplify compliance standards and all rules and regulations of applicable local, state and federal agencies including, but not limited to, Det Norske Veritas (DNV), Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA). Actively participates in outstanding customer service and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all.', N'Responsible for assisting with management of shift operations to ensure efficient movement of all requests for patient transports. This position functions as one member of a crew assigned to an ambulance and transports patients when necessary. Additionally, this role involves rounding with on-duty crews at outlying campuses, delivering supplies, assisting other crews with lifting and transporting patients, and rounding with staff at outlying Emergency Departments. In addition, this position inspects ambulances in service for cleanliness and preparedness. This role meets department metrics and standards of care, adheres to compliance standards, and all rules and regulations of applicable local, state, and federal agencies.', N'Responsible for assisting with management of shift operations to ensure efficient movement of all requests for patient transports. This position functions as one member of a crew assigned to an ambulance and transports patients when necessary. Additionally, this role involves rounding with on-duty crews at outlying campuses, delivering supplies, assisting other crews with lifting and transporting patients, and rounding with staff at outlying Emergency Departments. In addition, this position inspects ambulances in service for cleanliness and preparedness. This role meets department metrics and standards of care, adheres to compliance standards, and all rules and regulations of applicable local, state, and federal agencies.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Basic computer skills Required
•  Knowledge of service areas Required
•  Ambulance transport and budgetary knowledge Preferred

Education
• Technical/Vocational School Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 5+ driving passenger vehicles Required
•  1+ patient care experience Required

Licenses and Certifications
• Licensed Paramedic (PARA) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:05.8166667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:05.8166667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:05.8166667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (62, 62, 1, N'The Data Analyst analyzes various types of data and develops analyses and findings for resource allocation, financing, costs, and others', N'Responsible for analyzing various types of data to develop insights and findings that inform resource allocation, financing, and cost management. This position interprets data to provide actionable recommendations for improving efficiency and effectiveness. Additionally, this role collaborates with cross-functional teams to gather and validate data, ensuring accuracy and reliability. In addition, this position designs and maintains reports, dashboards, and visualizations to communicate key metrics and trends. Responsibilities for this role include identifying data patterns, performing statistical analyses, and presenting findings to stakeholders. Ensures data integrity and supports decision-making processes through thorough and precise analysis.', N'Responsible for analyzing various types of data to develop insights and findings that inform resource allocation, financing, and cost management. This position interprets data to provide actionable recommendations for improving efficiency and effectiveness. Additionally, this role collaborates with cross-functional teams to gather and validate data, ensuring accuracy and reliability. In addition, this position designs and maintains reports, dashboards, and visualizations to communicate key metrics and trends. Responsibilities for this role include identifying data patterns, performing statistical analyses, and presenting findings to stakeholders. Ensures data integrity and supports decision-making processes through thorough and precise analysis.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Ability to comprehend technical documentation Required
•  Ability to work independently Required
•  Ability to maintain confidentiality Required
•  Knowledge of database programs and spreadsheets Required
•  Knowledge of data extrapolation, interpretation and chart compilation Required
•  Ability to coordinate multiple priorities and issues to facilitate data needs Required
•  Ability to build reports for complex data analysis Required
•  Exceptional problem solving and organizational skills Required
•  Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Able to calculate statistical information and present it in user-friendly formats Preferred
•  Knowledge of Healthcare/Clinical operations Preferred
•  Experience in enterprise data platform strategy, establishing end to end data management technical architecture and providing corresponding roadmaps Required
•  Experience with Microsoft Power BI / Analytical tools Required
•  SQL Server, SSIS, SSRS, ETL tools Required
•  Must have effective communication skill, work ethic, attention to detail, time management skills and accountability Required
•  Design skills must be evident to produce reports with visual appeal that fit within our corporate template Required
•  Thorough understanding of investment data (accounting, performance, pricing, risk, etc.) Preferred
•  Programming skills (Python, R or MATLAB) and experience working with data Preferred
•  Knowledge of research methodology and statistical analysis Required
•  Proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Access) Required
•  Excellent written and oral communication skills Required
•  Interact effectively with a diverse, multicultural community Required
•  Work well under time constraints Required
•  Proficient in SPSS Preferred
•  Proficient in Qualtrics Preferred
•  Proficient in Adobe Preferred
•  Proficient in Crystal Reports Preferred
•  Strong computer software skills including advanced MS Excel skills (pivot tables, look ups, etc.) Required
•  Ability to learn new technology applications Required
•  Working knowledge of HPM report writing Required
•  Strong analytical skills Required
•  Excellent interpersonal skills Required
•  Well organized and detail-oriented Required
•  Knowledge of Medicare and state Medicaid program reimbursement laws and regulations Preferred
•  Proficient in use of regulatory cost reporting software Preferred

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 1+ experience Required
•  Experience in Post-Secondary Education Preferred
•  Experience with IPEDS reporting Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:07.8966667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:07.8966667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:07.8966667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (63, 63, 1, N'The Health Record System and Support Analyst (Chart Analyst) quantitatively analyzes inpatient and outpatient charts daily and accurately enters physician deficiencies into Cerner according to the department''s established policies.  Picks up medical records from the patient care units and reconciles receipt of all discharged patient records.  Processes pre-surgical records and imports them into patient charts after they are electronically faxed from physician offices, in partnership with other departments.  Participates and/or assists with other department functions, as requested.', N'Responsible for quantitatively analyzing inpatient and outpatient charts daily and accurately entering physician deficiencies into Cerner according to established policies. This position picks up medical records from patient care units and reconciles receipt of all discharged patient records. Additionally, this role processes pre-surgical records and imports them into patient charts after they are electronically faxed from physician offices, in partnership with other departments. In addition, this position participates and assists with other department functions as requested. Additionally, this role ensures compliance with departmental policies and procedures to maintain operational efficiency.', N'Responsible for quantitatively analyzing inpatient and outpatient charts daily and accurately entering physician deficiencies into Cerner according to established policies. This position picks up medical records from patient care units and reconciles receipt of all discharged patient records. Additionally, this role processes pre-surgical records and imports them into patient charts after they are electronically faxed from physician offices, in partnership with other departments. In addition, this position participates and assists with other department functions as requested. Additionally, this role ensures compliance with departmental policies and procedures to maintain operational efficiency.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Must have ability to set priorities and exercise independent judgement Required
•  Excellent skills with computer systems and the Cerner electronic medical record system Required
•  Proficiency with Microsoft Office including Word and Excel Required
•  Ability to communicate with all levels of associates, management, physicians, patients and other customers Required
•  Proven record of providing excellent customer service Required
•  Demonstrate excellent team skills Required
•  Ability to understand and prepare complex written materials, including spelling and grammar Required

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 1+ of previous work experience in healthcare setting Preferred 
• with computer systems Preferred 

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:09.9400000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:09.9400000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:09.9400000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (64, 64, 1, N'This position will have responsibility for receiving incoming supplies and equipment, putting away supplies in the storeroom, scanning receiving documents, delivering supplies to departments, handling returns to supplier, tagging equipment, and completing all associated computer software tasks to ensure accurate record keeping. The Supply Chain Receiving  Clerk ensures data in PeopleSoft is accurate and that system is properly used at their facility. Receiving  Clerks serve as materials gatekeepers for their hospital, ensuring the facility only pays for items that are received.', N'Responsible for receiving incoming supplies and equipment, putting away supplies in the storeroom, and scanning receiving documents. This position delivers supplies to departments, handles returns to suppliers, and tags equipment. Additionally, this role completes all associated computer software tasks to ensure accurate record keeping. In addition, this position ensures data in PeopleSoft is accurate and that the system is properly used. Additionally, this role serves as a materials gatekeeper for the hospital, ensuring the facility only pays for items that are received. Ensures all tasks are completed efficiently and accurately.', N'Responsible for receiving incoming supplies and equipment, putting away supplies in the storeroom, and scanning receiving documents. This position delivers supplies to departments, handles returns to suppliers, and tags equipment. Additionally, this role completes all associated computer software tasks to ensure accurate record keeping. In addition, this position ensures data in PeopleSoft is accurate and that the system is properly used. Additionally, this role serves as a materials gatekeeper for the hospital, ensuring the facility only pays for items that are received. Ensures all tasks are completed efficiently and accurately.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Critical thinking and analytical mindset Required
•  Possesses basic math skills. Required
•  Pays attention to detail. Required
•  Communicates clearly and effectively in English. Can communicate directly with delivery drivers. Required
•  Has computer skills and the ability to use a keypad and keyboard. Required
•  Can identify, sort and count accurately. Required
•  Exhibits familiarity with shipping and billing procedures. Required
