INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (65, 65, 1, N'This Supply Chain Lead Receiving Clerk will be responsible for performing the activities of the receiving department and occasionally supervising the work of Receiving Clerks and other receiving department staff. Receiving department activities include: receiving incoming supplies and equipment, putting away supplies in the storeroom, scanning receiving documents, delivering supplies to departments, handling returns to supplier, tagging equipment, and completing all associated computer software tasks to ensure accurate record keeping. The Supply Chain Lead Receiving Techs ensure data in PeopleSoft is accurate and that the system is properly used at their facility, and they serve as the materials gatekeepers for their hospital, ensuring the facility only pays for items that are actually received. The Supply Chain Lead Receiving Clerk is the lead point of contact within the receiving department in the absence of a manager or supervisor and may have responsibilities for processes and training related to the function.', N'Responsible for performing the activities of the receiving department and occasionally supervising the work of receiving department staff. This position handles receiving incoming supplies and equipment, putting away supplies in the storeroom, scanning receiving documents, delivering supplies to departments, handling returns to suppliers, tagging equipment, and completing all associated computer software tasks to ensure accurate record keeping. Additionally, this role ensures data in PeopleSoft is accurate and that the system is properly used at the facility, serving as the materials gatekeeper to ensure the facility only pays for items that are actually received. In addition, this position acts as the lead point of contact within the receiving department in the absence of a manager or supervisor. Additionally, this role may have responsibilities for processes and training related to the function.', N'Responsible for performing the activities of the receiving department and occasionally supervising the work of receiving department staff. This position handles receiving incoming supplies and equipment, putting away supplies in the storeroom, scanning receiving documents, delivering supplies to departments, handling returns to suppliers, tagging equipment, and completing all associated computer software tasks to ensure accurate record keeping. Additionally, this role ensures data in PeopleSoft is accurate and that the system is properly used at the facility, serving as the materials gatekeeper to ensure the facility only pays for items that are actually received. In addition, this position acts as the lead point of contact within the receiving department in the absence of a manager or supervisor. Additionally, this role may have responsibilities for processes and training related to the function.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Critical thinking and analytical mindset Required
•  Possesses basic math skills. Required
•  Pays attention to detail. Required
•  Communicates clearly and effectively in English. Can communicate directly with delivery drivers. Required
•  Has computer skills and the ability to use a keypad and keyboard. Required
