• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:13.8066667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:13.8066667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:13.8066667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (66, 66, 1, N'Reads patient records and, as needed, discusses patient conditions with physicians and/or clinical documentation improvement professionals to accurately and completely apply diagnostic, procedural and service codes to each patient condition treated (including operations) during an inpatient and outpatient encounter.  Abstracts clinical data from the patient record and enters into computer databases.  Serves as the source of clinical data for reimbursement, planning, and research.  Competently codes/abstracts inpatient and outpatient records', N'Responsible for reading patient records and discussing patient conditions with physicians and clinical documentation improvement professionals to accurately apply diagnostic, procedural, and service codes. This position abstracts clinical data from patient records and enters it into computer databases. Additionally, this role serves as the source of clinical data for reimbursement, planning, and research. In addition, this position competently codes and abstracts both inpatient and outpatient records. This role ensures the accuracy and completeness of coding for each patient condition treated. The position contributes to the overall efficiency and effectiveness of clinical data management.', N'Responsible for reading patient records and discussing patient conditions with physicians and clinical documentation improvement professionals to accurately apply diagnostic, procedural, and service codes. This position abstracts clinical data from patient records and enters it into computer databases. Additionally, this role serves as the source of clinical data for reimbursement, planning, and research. In addition, this position competently codes and abstracts both inpatient and outpatient records. This role ensures the accuracy and completeness of coding for each patient condition treated. The position contributes to the overall efficiency and effectiveness of clinical data management.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• A solid understanding of Medicare coding and billing requirements for hospital services is required.
•  Must possess excellent communication and problem solving skills.

Education
• Required

Field of Study
• Successful completion of inpatient (ICD-10-CM) and outpatient coding courses (CPT-4 / HCPCS)

Experience
• using coding software/encoder and other healthcare computer systems Required
•  in a prior coding position Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• Registered Health Information Administrator (RHIA) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:15.9066667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:15.9066667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:15.9066667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (67, 67, 1, N'Ensures timely processing and coding of outpatient laboratory tests/specimens, radiology/diagnostic imaging tests, etc. using ICD-10, Current Procedural Terminology (CPT)/HealthCare Common Procedure Coding System (CPT/HCPCS).', N'Responsible for ensuring timely processing and coding of outpatient laboratory tests, radiology, and diagnostic imaging tests using ICD-10, CPT, and HCPCS codes. This position accurately applies diagnostic, procedural, and service codes to patient records. Additionally, this role abstracts clinical data from patient records and enters it into computer databases. In addition, this position serves as the source of clinical data for reimbursement, planning, and research. This role ensures the accuracy and completeness of coding for each patient condition treated. The position contributes to the overall efficiency and effectiveness of clinical data management.', N'Responsible for ensuring timely processing and coding of outpatient laboratory tests, radiology, and diagnostic imaging tests using ICD-10, CPT, and HCPCS codes. This position accurately applies diagnostic, procedural, and service codes to patient records. Additionally, this role abstracts clinical data from patient records and enters it into computer databases. In addition, this position serves as the source of clinical data for reimbursement, planning, and research. This role ensures the accuracy and completeness of coding for each patient condition treated. The position contributes to the overall efficiency and effectiveness of clinical data management.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Basic clerical skills (typing, filing, phone skills) and basic computer skills Preferred
•  One year of experience with computer input procedures. Preferred
•  Must possess positive communication and customer service skills Preferred
•  Must be proficient in the English language Preferred

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• or General Education Development (GED)

Experience
• 2+ of outpatient coding experience in an outpatient healthcare facility, acute/ambulatory care facility using ICD-10-CM and CPT-4 sources. Required

Licenses and Certifications
• Certified Billing and Coding Specialist (CBCS) Preferred

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:17.9466667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:17.9466667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:17.9466667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (68, 68, 1, N'The Supply Chain Analyst is responsible for providing analytical and administrative support, as well as inventory management assistance, to the facility team. The Supply Chain Analyst is responsible for various analytical and administrative duties, which may include processing requisitions and purchase orders, performing cycle counts, updating  the warehouse and par locations, communicating with vendors, and generating inventory reports and cost and value analyses. The Analyst coordinates product conversions with the Clinical Resource Manager, receives reports from and partners on data analytics efforts with the Corporate Analysts, and completes ad hoc projects for the Supply Chain Director.', N'Responsible for providing analytical and administrative support, as well as inventory management assistance, to the facility team. This position processes requisitions and purchase orders, performs cycle counts, updates warehouse and par locations, communicates with vendors, and generates inventory reports and cost and value analyses. Additionally, this role coordinates product conversions with the Clinical Resource Manager and partners on data analytics efforts with Corporate Analysts. In addition, this position completes ad hoc projects for the Supply Chain Director. Responsibilities for this role include various analytical and administrative duties. This position ensures efficient supply chain operations and supports the overall facility team.', N'Responsible for providing analytical and administrative support, as well as inventory management assistance, to the facility team. This position processes requisitions and purchase orders, performs cycle counts, updates warehouse and par locations, communicates with vendors, and generates inventory reports and cost and value analyses. Additionally, this role coordinates product conversions with the Clinical Resource Manager and partners on data analytics efforts with Corporate Analysts. In addition, this position completes ad hoc projects for the Supply Chain Director. Responsibilities for this role include various analytical and administrative duties. This position ensures efficient supply chain operations and supports the overall facility team.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Proficient use of Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Access, Word, PowerPoint) Required
•  Ability to effectively communicate (orally and in writing) Required
•  Ability to analyze financial data and generate reports Required
•  Ability to manage multiple projects with competing priorities Required
•  Knowledge and experience in performing the duties associated with purchasing, receiving, shipping, and distribution Preferred
•  Competence using materials management/ERP systems such as PeopleSoft Preferred

Education
• Associate Required

Field of Study
• N/A

Experience
• 3+ years experience Required
•  Six (6) - (12) months ERP and/or analytics experience Preferred

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:19.9666667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:19.9666667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:19.9666667' AS DateTime2))
