Field of Study
• In health information management or a related field
•  In health information management or a related field

Experience
• in administrative and staff management Required 
• in project management Required 

Licenses and Certifications
• Registered Health Information Administrator (RHIA) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:36.1166667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:36.1166667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:36.1166667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (77, 77, 1, N'The Regional Neurodiagnostics Manager is responsible for managing the daily operations of all assigned departments across the region.  Provide professional and technical support to staff, physicians, and leadership to ensure efficient daily departmental operations. Provide training to team members and other clinical areas as needed. Analyze workloads/workflows and assigns staff to meet demand and improve operational efficiency. Facilitate and track all aspects of reporting, including quality assurance, performance improvement, regulatory compliance, financial reports and other reports as needed. Develop and implement policies, procedures and guidelines to ensure operational efficiency and compliance with hospital, and regulatory agencies.   Establish and maintain ethical working relationships and good rapport with stakeholders, such as physicians, hospital staff, and commercial agencies.  Meet with customers, partners, and team members to assure service levels are maintained. Actively participate in outstanding customer service and accept responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all. Adhere to the Emplify Health Corporate Compliance Plan and to rules and regulations of applicable local, state, and federal agencies and accrediting bodies.', N'Responsible for managing the daily operations of all assigned departments across the region. This position provides professional and technical support to staff, physicians, and leadership to ensure efficient departmental operations. Additionally, this role provides training to team members and other clinical areas as needed. In addition, this position analyzes workloads and workflows, assigns staff to meet demand, and improves operational efficiency. Additionally, this role facilitates and tracks all aspects of reporting, including quality assurance, performance improvement, regulatory compliance, and financial reports. Develops and implements policies, procedures, and guidelines to ensure operational efficiency and compliance with hospital and regulatory agencies.', N'Responsible for managing the daily operations of all assigned departments across the region. This position provides professional and technical support to staff, physicians, and leadership to ensure efficient departmental operations. Additionally, this role provides training to team members and other clinical areas as needed. In addition, this position analyzes workloads and workflows, assigns staff to meet demand, and improves operational efficiency. Additionally, this role facilitates and tracks all aspects of reporting, including quality assurance, performance improvement, regulatory compliance, and financial reports. Develops and implements policies, procedures, and guidelines to ensure operational efficiency and compliance with hospital and regulatory agencies.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Comprehensive knowledge and application of principles of clinical Neurodiagnostics Required
•  Strong written and verbal communication skills and can effectively work with people of diverse backgrounds Required
•  Excellent customer service and problem-solving skills Required
•  Ability to function independently with little or no supervision Required
•  Ability to manage and lead teams Required
•  Comfortable with public speaking/presentations to groups of varying sizes Required
•  Good understanding of financial reports and concepts Required
•  Business software proficiency, particularly Microsoft Office suite and EPIC Required

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• in Health Administration, Business Administration, or a similar field, or supervisory/leadership experience may be substituted on a year-to-year basis in lieu of degree
•  Graduate of a school of Electroneurodiagnostic (END) Technology OR on-the-job training program

Experience
• 5+ END technical experience in a hospital setting with progressive growth Required 
• 3+  Leadership/management experience Required 
• Experience supervising a Seizure Monitoring Unit or Center for Sleep Disorders Preferred 

Licenses and Certifications
• Registered Electroencephalography Technician (REEGT) through ABRET Neurodiagnostic Credentialing and Accreditation For EGG/EMU positions only Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• Certification as a Registered Polysomnographic Technologist through the American Board of Sleep Medicine (ABSM) OR Board of Registered Polysomnographic Technologists (BRPT) For Sleep positions only  Required
• Registrations in multiple modalities, which could include Sleep, EEG, Long Term Monitoring, and/or Intra-operative Monitoring  Preferred', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:38.1000000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:38.1000000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:38.1000000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (78, 78, 1, N'This position will have responsibility for the supply replenishment process of par locations; this includes straightening, counting, picking, and stocking supplies for specific areas then completing any paperwork or computer software tasks needed to account for inventory movement. This role serves as a representative of Supply Chain to clinicians in their assigned areas; as such this role must be attentive to providing excellent customer service which includes working collaboratively with customers to facilitate and manage the supply replenishment process and  managing par level changes as needed. The Supply Chain Distribution Tech may also be responsible for assisting in picking and delivering supplies to non-assigned departments upon request, picking up items for return and general upkeep of the inventory storeroom.

The Supply Chain Lead Distribution Tech also acts as a representative of the supply chain to clinical staff and should be attentive to clinician''s needs and provide excellent customer service to the departments they support. This role may include supervisory responsibilities such as managing the training and evaluation of distribution staff members.', N'Responsible for the supply replenishment process of par locations, including straightening, counting, picking, and stocking supplies for specific areas, and completing any paperwork or computer software tasks needed to account for inventory movement. This position serves as a representative of Supply Chain to clinicians in assigned areas, providing excellent customer service and working collaboratively with customers to manage the supply replenishment process and par level changes. Additionally, this role assists in picking and delivering supplies to non-assigned departments upon request, picking up items for return, and maintaining the inventory storeroom. In addition, this position may include supervisory responsibilities such as managing the training and evaluation of distribution staff members. Additionally, this role acts as a representative of the supply chain to clinical staff, being attentive to clinician''s needs and providing excellent customer service. Ensures the efficient and accurate performance of assigned duties to support the overall supply chain operations.', N'Responsible for the supply replenishment process of par locations, including straightening, counting, picking, and stocking supplies for specific areas, and completing any paperwork or computer software tasks needed to account for inventory movement. This position serves as a representative of Supply Chain to clinicians in assigned areas, providing excellent customer service and working collaboratively with customers to manage the supply replenishment process and par level changes. Additionally, this role assists in picking and delivering supplies to non-assigned departments upon request, picking up items for return, and maintaining the inventory storeroom. In addition, this position may include supervisory responsibilities such as managing the training and evaluation of distribution staff members. Additionally, this role acts as a representative of the supply chain to clinical staff, being attentive to clinician''s needs and providing excellent customer service. Ensures the efficient and accurate performance of assigned duties to support the overall supply chain operations.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Possesses basic math skills. Required
•  Pays attention to detail. Required
•  Communicates clearly and effectively in English. Can communicate directly with clinicians. Required
•  Has computer skills, including Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook. Required
•  Can identify, sort and count accurately. Required
•  Demonstrated ability to use an ERP system. Preferred
•  Understands medical terminology and products. Preferred
•  Demonstrates knowledge of inventory, receiving, replenishment and par level concepts. Preferred
•  Ability to operate material handling equipment. Preferred
•  Minimum of 6 months experience in a supply chain environment. Required
•  Minimum of 6 months experience in a customer service setting. Required

Education
• High School Grad or Equiv Required

Field of Study
• OR 2+ years of ERP experience Required

Experience
• N/A

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:40.1966667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:40.1966667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:40.1966667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (79, 79, 1, N'Performs Radiographic imaging procedures. Positions, moves, and assists patients. Performs clerical duties. Performs basic patient care within scope of practice and to departmental standards. Responsibility to adhere to the Hospital Corporate compliance plan, to the rules and regulations of all local, state, and Federal agencies, and to the standards of all accrediting bodies.', N'Responsible for performing radiographic imaging procedures. This position positions, moves, and assists patients. Additionally, this role performs clerical duties and basic patient care within the scope of practice and departmental standards. In addition, this position adheres to the Hospital Corporate compliance plan. Additionally, this role follows the rules and regulations of all local, state, and Federal agencies. Ensures compliance with the standards of all accrediting bodies.', N'Responsible for performing radiographic imaging procedures. This position positions, moves, and assists patients. Additionally, this role performs clerical duties and basic patient care within the scope of practice and departmental standards. In addition, this position adheres to the Hospital Corporate compliance plan. Additionally, this role follows the rules and regulations of all local, state, and Federal agencies. Ensures compliance with the standards of all accrediting bodies.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Ability to analyze and assess data, techniques, methodology, equipment operation, and quality control to ensure that information is obtained and presented accurately Required
•  Up-to-date knowledge of patient positioning and equipment operations, including x-ray producing equipment, if applicable per facility Required
•  Ability to communicate appropriately and effectively with patients and their family, hospital staff, nurses, physicians, and other health care professionals Required
•  Knowledge of commonly used concepts, practices, and procedures in the health care industry Required
•  Able to fully use all Radiographic and fluoroscopic equipment Required
•  Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required

Education
• Associate Required

Field of Study
• or equivalent two years of experience in a related field
•  Graduate of accredited Radiologic Science program

Experience
• 2+ years experience Required

Licenses and Certifications
• Basic Cardiac Life Support (BCLS) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:42.2966667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:42.2966667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:42.2966667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (80, 80, 1, N'The Office of Design and Construction (ODC) Assistant Project Coordinator (APC) works under the ODC Project Manager Sr. II and Project Manager(s) on all projects assigned. The APC coordinates, expedites, and distributes project information including changes in project priorities with respect to schedule, performance and budget. The APC manages multiple small construction projects (under $5,000) under the supervision of an ODC Project Coordinator or Project Manager. Actively participates in outstanding customer service and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all.', N'Responsible for coordinating, expediting, and distributing project information for all assigned projects. This position manages multiple small construction projects under $5,000 under supervision. Additionally, this role ensures changes in project priorities are communicated effectively with respect to schedule, performance, and budget. In addition, this position actively participates in providing outstanding customer service. Responsibilities for this role include maintaining respectful relationships with all parties involved. This role contributes to the efficient execution of projects within the Office of Design and Construction.', N'Responsible for coordinating, expediting, and distributing project information for all assigned projects. This position manages multiple small construction projects under $5,000 under supervision. Additionally, this role ensures changes in project priorities are communicated effectively with respect to schedule, performance, and budget. In addition, this position actively participates in providing outstanding customer service. Responsibilities for this role include maintaining respectful relationships with all parties involved. This role contributes to the efficient execution of projects within the Office of Design and Construction.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Knowledge of design and construction techniques Required
•  Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Knowledge of healthcare design and construction techniques Preferred
•  Proficient in e-Builder software program Preferred
•  Proficient in Microsoft Project or similar project management system Preferred

Education
• Associate Preferred

Field of Study
• in Interior Design, Architecture, Engineering, Construction Management or related field.

Experience
• 3+ construction administration experience or equivalent combination of education and experience Required 
• Experience with Agency for Health Care Administration (AHCA, or equivalent state agency) construction requirements Preferred 

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 11, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:44.1600000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:44.1600000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:44.1600000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (81, 81, 1, N'Manages daily operations and develops, implements, and monitors plans for patient care services in the imaging department.', N'Responsible for managing daily operations and developing, implementing, and monitoring plans for patient care services in the imaging department. This position ensures efficient workflow and high-quality patient care. Additionally, this role oversees the coordination of imaging services and collaborates with other healthcare professionals. In addition, this position monitors compliance with regulatory standards and departmental policies. Additionally, this role addresses any issues related to patient care and service delivery. This position contributes to the overall effectiveness and improvement of the imaging department.', N'Responsible for managing daily operations and developing, implementing, and monitoring plans for patient care services in the imaging department. This position ensures efficient workflow and high-quality patient care. Additionally, this role oversees the coordination of imaging services and collaborates with other healthcare professionals. In addition, this position monitors compliance with regulatory standards and departmental policies. Additionally, this role addresses any issues related to patient care and service delivery. This position contributes to the overall effectiveness and improvement of the imaging department.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Must show evidence of job-specific competencies.
•  Must have excellent interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills.
•  Computer literacy in Word, Excel, Outlook, and Internet access.
•  Previous Business Development experience.
•  Must be able to speak, read and write English.
•  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.
•  Effective oral and written communication skills, with the ability to articulate complex information in understandable terms to all levels of staff.
•  Business software proficiency, particularly Microsoft Office Suite, and experience with Cerner and PACS preferred.
•  Ability to work in a matrix-management environment to achieve organizational goals.
•  Performance improvement skills.
•  Ability to interact effectively with patients and families under physical and/or emotional stress.
•  Knowledge of Medical Terminology.
•  Hospital, Medical Practice, or Physician office experience.
•  Ability to acquire and effectively apply knowledge relating to specific processes, techniques, and procedures.
•  Demonstrates flexibility and willingness to adapt to diverse roles within the department and leadership team.
•  Up-to-date knowledge of department-specific hazards, such as ionizing radiation and universal precautions, to adhere to safety standards established by healthcare regulatory agencies.
•  Annual planning  budget and project experience.
•  Prior success in working with teams/managing people.
•  Ability to analyze and assess data, techniques, methodology, equipment operation, and quality control to ensure information quality.
•  Basic computer skills and advanced knowledge and experience with Word and Excel.
•  Imaging management, experience working with physicians, formal project management experience, and clinical experience within Imaging preferred.
•  Demonstrates leadership and teaching skills.
•  Knowledge of all aspects of department functions for adequate supervision and direction of staff.
•  Ability to perform technical procedures without supervision.
•  Knowledge of communication styles and proper engagement behaviors with patients, staff, and physicians.
•  LEAN training preferred.
•  Attention to detail and accuracy.
•  Multitasking ability.
•  Knowledge of basic state and federal laws as applicable to healthcare settings.
•  Ability to deal efficiently, ethically, and courteously with all patients, physicians, and hospital personnel.
•  Strong knowledge of financial and business aspects of imaging.

Education
• Associate Required

Field of Study
• in Healthcare Administration, Health Services or Business Administration
•  in Healthcare Administration, Health Services or Business Administration

Experience
• 1+ of leadership/management experience Required

Licenses and Certifications
• Basic Life Support - CPR Cert (BLS) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:46.0933333' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:46.0933333' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:46.0933333' AS DateTime2))
