 Department.', N'Responsible for the supervision and management of daily pharmacy operations and activities in the Pharmacy Department. This position ensures the delivery of quality patient care through the implementation and maintenance of medication preparation and distribution services. Additionally, this role assures effective supervision, staff development, appropriate staffing, and promotes positive employee and guest relations. In addition, this position establishes and maintains effective communication lines with other departments and outside entities, integrating Pharmacy activities and objectives through the development and implementation of policies and procedures. This role assures well-organized workflow and maintains labor productivity and financial data within the Pharmacy Department.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Demonstrate ability to work in a collaborative environment and adapt easily to change Required
•  Demonstrate excellent time management skills Required
•  Must be able to read, write and speak conversational English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Understanding of medication safety systems and just culture Preferred

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• completion of residency in health systems administration and leadership

Experience
• of hospital experience
•  previous experience in hospital management
• 
• Preferred qualification for state of employment will be required

Licenses and Certifications
• Pharmacy Consultant (PHARMCON) Preferred

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• Consultant Pharmacy License if applicable by jurisdiction.  Preferred', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:51.6900000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:51.6900000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:51.6900000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (85, 85, 1, N'The Director of Facility Design & Construction is responsible for the direction and management of personnel, finances, fiscal planning, development and implementation of programs, policies & procedures related to the maintenance, repair, changes and additions to the organizations physical plants, grounds and utility systems. Is responsible for the design of multiple projects as assigned, with or without consultants, interfacing with clinical and engineering staff, management of code compliance, and commissioning of the building.  These responsibilities usually involve the management of employees of Well 65+, consultant designers, contractors, and often other individuals with expert skills in their field. Actively participates in outstanding customer service and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all. Directs the operational and strategic activities of the Facility Infrastructure Crew as the team manages multiple projects of varying sizes, from pre-construction planning stages through build-out. Works closely on strategic planning and prioritization of projects with campus administration, finance directors, facility directors and has oversight of multiple vendors, contractors, and Well65+ staff', N'Responsible for the direction and management of personnel, finances, fiscal planning, and the development and implementation of programs, policies, and procedures related to the maintenance, repair, changes, and additions to the organization''s physical plants, grounds, and utility systems. This role designs multiple projects as assigned, with or without consultants, interfacing with clinical and engineering staff, managing code compliance, and commissioning buildings. Additionally, this position manages employees, consultant designers, contractors, and other individuals with expert skills in their field. In addition, this position directs the operational and strategic activities of the Facility Infrastructure Crew as the team manages multiple projects of varying sizes, from pre-construction planning stages through build-out. Additionally, this role works closely on strategic planning and prioritization of projects with campus administration, finance directors, facility directors, and oversees multiple vendors, contractors, and staff.', N'Responsible for the direction and management of personnel, finances, fiscal planning, and the development and implementation of programs, policies, and procedures related to the maintenance, repair, changes, and additions to the organization''s physical plants, grounds, and utility systems. This role designs multiple projects as assigned, with or without consultants, interfacing with clinical and engineering staff, managing code compliance, and commissioning buildings. Additionally, this position manages employees, consultant designers, contractors, and other individuals with expert skills in their field. In addition, this position directs the operational and strategic activities of the Facility Infrastructure Crew as the team manages multiple projects of varying sizes, from pre-construction planning stages through build-out. Additionally, this role works closely on strategic planning and prioritization of projects with campus administration, finance directors, facility directors, and oversees multiple vendors, contractors, and staff.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Extensive knowledge of facilities planning, capital and operating budget development, facilities operations and maintenance, and/or facilities management in a healthcare setting Required
•  Knowledge of utilities management Required
•  Excellent project management skills to manage multiple small to mid-sized healthcare projects Required
•  Knowledge of healthcare design and construction techniques Required
•  Ability to read and interpret construction drawings and contracts Required
•  Knowledge of the principles, theories, and practices of large mechanical systems such as HVAC, plumbing, electrical (MEP) systems, and engineering maintenance, including ability to problem solve effectively. Required
•  Excellent financial analysis, strategic planning and problem-solving skills required Required
•  Understanding of accounting, budgeting and business management practices Required
•  Knowledge of computer applications in facilities design, facilities operations and administrative management, laws governing facilities operations including environmental protection, occupational safety and human accommodations, etc. Required
•  Effective computer skills, particularly Microsoft Office Outlook, Word, Excel Required
•  Excellent written and verbal communications skills (i.e., organizing and clarifying complex issues, translating messages into clearly understood writing or speech, etc.) Required
•  Strong interpersonal skills with ability to work with and manage multi-faceted teams Required
•  Excellent oral and written communication skills, with the ability to articulate complex information in understandable terms to all levels of staff. Required
•  Ability to build and maintain effective and productive teams. Required
•  Proficiency in managing a group of diverse activities and competing interests Required
•  Skill in leading, administering, managing, and directing others in a service-oriented environment Required
•  Comfortable in making presentations to management and customers Required
•  Skill in developing and maintaining internal and external relationship involving difficult, formal negotiations Preferred
•  Proficiency in the use of computer aided design software (AutoCAD) Preferred

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• in Architecture, Engineering, Construction Management, or related field
•  in Architecture, Engineering, Construction Management or related field

Experience
• 7+ project management experience Required 
• Extensive experience in all phases of architectural design Required 
• Extensive experience in the construction process, including all project deliverables Required 
• Experience with Agency for Health Care Administration (AHCA, or equivalent state agency) construction requirements  Required 

Licenses and Certifications
• Project Management Professional (PMP) Preferred

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 11, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:53.5100000' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:53.5100000' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:53.5100000' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (86, 86, 1, N'The Senior Manager of Transition Strategy and Implementation, reporting to the Director of Operations, works in collaboration with Practice Leaders, Network Development, Strategy and all internal departments to facilitate practice transitions. The Senior Manager of Transition Strategy and Implementation will be responsible for all duties and set up related to practice openings, closures, relocations, and acquisitions.', N'Responsible for facilitating practice transitions in collaboration with Practice Leaders, Network Development, Strategy, and all internal departments. This position manages all duties and setup related to practice openings, closures, relocations, and acquisitions. Additionally, this role ensures efficient and effective execution of transition strategies. In addition, this position coordinates with various teams to support seamless practice integration. Ensures all transitions are completed in alignment with organizational goals and standards.', N'Responsible for facilitating practice transitions in collaboration with Practice Leaders, Network Development, Strategy, and all internal departments. This position manages all duties and setup related to practice openings, closures, relocations, and acquisitions. Additionally, this role ensures efficient and effective execution of transition strategies. In addition, this position coordinates with various teams to support seamless practice integration. Ensures all transitions are completed in alignment with organizational goals and standards.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Demonstrates the ability to collaborate with all departments for adherence to the plan, rules and regulations of applicable federal, state, and local regulatory and/or accrediting agencies Required
•  Demonstrates business and human resource skills as they relate to assigned areas of service Required
•  Demonstrates competency in regards to communication and relationship building Required
•  Ability to act independently and be self-motivated Required
•  Is a role model for professionalism Required
•  Knowledge of organizational policies, regulations and procedures Required
•  May travel 75-100% of time Required
•  Experience with strategy and practice transition processes Preferred
•  Experience with Project Management Preferred

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• in Healthcare Administration, Business or related field
•  in Healthcare Administration, Business or related field

Experience
• 2+ experience in healthcare operations Preferred 
• Experience with large multi-specialty physician group Preferred 

Licenses and Certifications
• N/A

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:55.5966667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:55.5966667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:55.5966667' AS DateTime2))
INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (87, 87, 1, N'"The Centralized Payment Posting team is responsible for payment posting activities for the majority of Emplify services provided.  Under minimal supervision of the Director of the Payment Reconciliation Center, the Payment Manager coordinates and manages the cash control functions, including but not limited to posting insurance and patient payments, managing patient refunds and credit balances, patient and insurance correspondence, reconciliation, and other miscellaneous functions. The Manager provides direction and support to staff, promotes staff development, and collaborates with other managers, directors, and administrative staff to help ensure operations function in a safe, effective, and fiscally responsible manner. The Manager creates a clear vision for the future and defines the values that underlie the day to day activities of assigned functions. Additional responsibilities include analysis and resolution of problems related to their areas of assignment as well as personnel activities including hiring, training, development, and termination of assigned supervisors / staff. The Manager is also responsible to maintain a working knowledge of core functions throughout the Reconciliation Services department.



The Manager works closely with other Reconciliation Services teams to help ensure efficient and timely processes and provides detailed feedback to the Director regarding team performance. This position is responsible for monitoring payment and adjustment trends, specifically significant changes and/or any anomalies. This position monitors and interprets reports and dashboards, including payment reports, monthly A/R, reconciliation reports and all other reports and dashboards as necessary. The Manager helps ensure the timeliness and appropriateness of posting payments. The Manager works closely with Emplify Information Technology (AIT) resources, clearinghouses, insurance payers, and bank vendors to help ensure the highest level of technology and automation is being utilized throughout the payment posting functions."', N'Responsible for coordinating and managing cash control functions, including posting insurance and patient payments, managing patient refunds and credit balances, patient and insurance correspondence, reconciliation, and other miscellaneous functions. This position provides direction and support to staff, promotes staff development, and collaborates with other managers, directors, and administrative staff to ensure operations function in a safe, effective, and fiscally responsible manner. Additionally, this role monitors payment and adjustment trends, interprets reports and dashboards, and ensures the timeliness and appropriateness of posting payments. In addition, this position works closely with IT resources, clearinghouses, insurance payers, and bank vendors to ensure the highest level of technology and automation is utilized throughout the payment posting functions. Contributes to the overall improvement of the department through analysis and resolution of problems related to assigned areas.', N'Responsible for coordinating and managing cash control functions, including posting insurance and patient payments, managing patient refunds and credit balances, patient and insurance correspondence, reconciliation, and other miscellaneous functions. This position provides direction and support to staff, promotes staff development, and collaborates with other managers, directors, and administrative staff to ensure operations function in a safe, effective, and fiscally responsible manner. Additionally, this role monitors payment and adjustment trends, interprets reports and dashboards, and ensures the timeliness and appropriateness of posting payments. In addition, this position works closely with IT resources, clearinghouses, insurance payers, and bank vendors to ensure the highest level of technology and automation is utilized throughout the payment posting functions. Contributes to the overall improvement of the department through analysis and resolution of problems related to assigned areas.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• " General knowledge of insurance billing practices, including Provider Level Balance (PLB) adjustments
•  Understanding of file formatting and interpretation of insurance Explanation of Benefits (EOB)
•  Clear understanding of payer adjudication and file flow that may include clearinghouses and other third party intermediaries.
•  Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing
•  Technical Skills
•  Extensive Knowledge on use of email, search engine, Internet
•  Ability to effectively navigate payer websites
•  Knowledge and use of Microsoft Products
•   Outlook
•   Word
•   Excel
•   Teams
•   OneNote"
•  " General working knowledge of accounting principles and General Ledger systems as it relates to the revenue cycle
•  Experience with ERP systems (e.g. PeopleSoft)
•  Experience with various patient accounting systems
•   NextGen
•   AthenaHealth
•   Cerner
•   HomeCare Homebase
•  Working knowledge of Epic Practice Management System"

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• in Healthcare Administration, Finance, Business Administration or equivalent degree

Experience
• 4+  of experience in healthcare revenue cycle or payment posting operations Required 
• 2+ of experience working as a manager, supervisor or lead with direct reports Required 
• 4+ accredited university or college or an Associate degree plus 3 years of relevant experience, or an additional 4 years of relevant experience in Finance, Revenue Cycle, or reconciliation. Preferred 

Licenses and Certifications
• EPIC Credential (EPIC CRED) Resolute Billing certification and/or other relevant Epic certifications." Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• N/A', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:58.2066667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:58.2066667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:23:58.2066667' AS DateTime2))
