INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (89, 89, 1, N'The Executive Director of Nursing is responsible for developing and leading comprehensive methods to direct the execution of multiple and interrelated programs and top initiatives required for the achievement of Emplify strategic vision. This critical role is accountable for system-wide program oversight, prioritized escalation, timeline visibility and knowledge transfer. Programs and initiatives may include, but are not limited to Clinical Excellence, Critical Care, Nursing, Emergency Services, Workforce Planning, Care Transformation and Mission Integration. The Executive director must collaborate with executives and leaders across all corporate functions and operational divisions to facilitate, coordinate and implement the development and execution of strategic initiatives that are aligned with our 2030 company aspirations.  This individual must have the mental agility to be both a strategic thinker and a tactical leader, capable of understanding and communicating alignment of initiatives to the Vision as well as project objectives, value propositions and resource requirements.', N'Responsible for developing and leading comprehensive methods to direct the execution of multiple and interrelated programs and top initiatives required for the achievement of strategic vision. This role is accountable for system-wide program oversight, prioritized escalation, timeline visibility, and knowledge transfer. Additionally, this position collaborates with executives and leaders across all corporate functions and operational divisions to facilitate, coordinate, and implement the development and execution of strategic initiatives. In addition, this position manages programs and initiatives including Clinical Excellence, Critical Care, Nursing, Emergency Services, Workforce Planning, Care Transformation, and Mission Integration. This role requires mental agility to be both a strategic thinker and a tactical leader, capable of understanding and communicating alignment of initiatives to the Vision as well as project objectives, value propositions, and resource requirements.', N'Responsible for developing and leading comprehensive methods to direct the execution of multiple and interrelated programs and top initiatives required for the achievement of strategic vision. This role is accountable for system-wide program oversight, prioritized escalation, timeline visibility, and knowledge transfer. Additionally, this position collaborates with executives and leaders across all corporate functions and operational divisions to facilitate, coordinate, and implement the development and execution of strategic initiatives. In addition, this position manages programs and initiatives including Clinical Excellence, Critical Care, Nursing, Emergency Services, Workforce Planning, Care Transformation, and Mission Integration. This role requires mental agility to be both a strategic thinker and a tactical leader, capable of understanding and communicating alignment of initiatives to the Vision as well as project objectives, value propositions, and resource requirements.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• " In-depth knowledge of clinical/hospital operations Required
•  Knowledge of continuum of care quality standards and regulations Required
•  Ability to conduct primary and secondary research and to analyze and synthesize data from multiple sources. Required
•  Expertise in developing new programs Required
•  Ability to design, structure, implement and oversee multiple projects and teams simultaneously and effectively collaborate with cross-functional teams and external parties, including executives, employees, physicians and consumers. Required
•  Ability to identify opportunities and solve problems. Required
•  Demonstrated background in strategic analysis and planning. Required
•  Strong attention to detail and ability to organize and synthesize a broad set of information. Required
•  Excellent judgment, analytical and interpersonal skills, and written, presentation and verbal communication skills Required
•  Strong understanding of business management. Required
•  Ability to work in a matrix-management environment to achieve organizational goals. Required
•  Strong understanding and knowledge of the general principles and practices of healthcare administration and the healthcare industry Required
•  Expert proficiency in the use of Microsoft Office and proficiency in Visio and databases" Required
•  Experience with/knowledge of healthcare trends, legislative agendas Preferred

Education
• Master''s of Nursing Required

Field of Study
• MSN or equivalent

Experience
• 10+ management experience or equivalent Required 
• Experience working with diverse teams, managing major events and projects Required 
• 10+ management experience or equivalent Preferred 
• Experience in strategic planning Preferred 
• Experience in mentoring project managers Preferred 
• 10+ management experience or equivalent Preferred 
• Experience in strategic planning Preferred 
• Experience in mentoring project managers" Preferred 

Licenses and Certifications
• Registered Nurse (RN) Required

Additional Licenses and Certifications
• Portfolio Management Professional (PMP)  Preferred
• National Board Certification in a clinical specialty  Required
• DNP or Nursing PhD  Preferred
• Change Management (Prosci) certification"IENCE  Preferred', NULL, 0, 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:24:02.1566667' AS DateTime2), 1, CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:24:02.1566667' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2025-06-20T05:24:02.1566667' AS DateTime2))
