INSERT [dbo].[job_descriptions] ([id], [job_id], [version], [job_summary_original], [job_summary_ai], [job_summary_changes], [other_job_description], [comments], [is_critical], [last_edited_by_id], [last_updated_date], [is_active], [created_at], [updated_at]) VALUES (92, 92, 1, N'The registered dietitian utilizes the nutrition care process to screen, assess, diagnose, offer nutrition intervention, and monitor the nutrition status and progress of patients. The registered dietitian uses the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics Standards of Practice in Nutrition Care and Standards of Professional Performance for registered dietitians. Actively participates in outstanding customer service and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all.', N'Responsible for utilizing the nutrition care process to screen, assess, diagnose, offer nutrition intervention, and monitor the nutrition status and progress of patients. This position uses the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics Standards of Practice in Nutrition Care and Standards of Professional Performance for registered dietitians. Additionally, this role actively participates in providing outstanding customer service. In addition, this position accepts responsibility in maintaining respectful relationships with all. Responsibilities for this role include ensuring accurate nutrition assessments, providing effective interventions, and monitoring patient progress. Contributes to the overall efficiency and effectiveness of patient care through diligent performance of assigned duties.', N'Responsible for utilizing the nutrition care process to screen, assess, diagnose, offer nutrition intervention, and monitor the nutrition status and progress of patients. This position uses the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics Standards of Practice in Nutrition Care and Standards of Professional Performance for registered dietitians. Additionally, this role actively participates in providing outstanding customer service. In addition, this position accepts responsibility in maintaining respectful relationships with all. Responsibilities for this role include ensuring accurate nutrition assessments, providing effective interventions, and monitoring patient progress. Contributes to the overall efficiency and effectiveness of patient care through diligent performance of assigned duties.', N'Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Must be able to read, write, speak, and have good comprehension of conversational English Required
•  Basic computer skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office Required
•  Comprehensive knowledge and application of nutrition services and medical nutrition therapy Required
•  General knowledge of nutrient analysis, word processing, e-mail, and spreadsheet software Required
•  Ability to search the web for nutrition research or practice updates and apply knowledge to updating reference materials, preparing for presentations, education, etc. Required
•  Avails self to staff on units as the nutrition expert Required
•  Performs Meal Test Trays 3 times per month (breakfast, lunch, dinner) Required
•  Attends interdisciplinary meetings and rounds on assigned units as scheduled unless valid excuse demonstrated Required
•  Assists in regulatory survey preparation when applicable Required
•  Reviews and/or updates department resource/reference materials when applicable or required Required
•  When confronted with barriers to meeting patient care standards, improves process by planning and implementing action steps Required
•  Identifies specific patient or staff needs, initiates and develops educational or clinical materials then evaluates outcomes Required
•  Assures that care delivered to each patient is in accordance with established standards Required
•  Skill and knowledge in working with an electronic health record system Required
•  Analyzes and interprets reliable assessment data to identify an actual occurrence, risk of, or potential for developing a nutrition problem Required
•  Nutrition Diagnoses/Problems are included on the patient care plan and updated as more data becomes available, or signed off as applicable Required
•  Provides appropriate intervention in accordance with the identified patients goals Required
•  Identifies and follows through with potential complex discharge planning needs, intervenes early to promote timely attainment of goals Required
•  Adheres to reassessment timeframe per standards Required
•  Reassesses and updates nutrition care process and implement changes as indicated Required
•  Complies with National Patient Safety Goals regarding abbreviation usage, patient identification Required
•  Assessment, interventions and procedures utilizing equipment are appropriate for age group Required
•  Strong verbal and written communication, organizational, problem-solving, and customer service skills Required
•  Ability to interact constructively with supervisors, peers, and support personnel Required
•  Ability to work well with minimal supervision Required
•  Ability to keep accurate and complete records Required
•  Initiative to keep abreast of new information/products/developments in the field of Dietetics Required
•  Knowledge of federal, state, and local laws and regulations as related to Dietetics practice Required
•  Proficiency in the Nutrition Care Process of the Academy of Nutrition & Dietetics Required
•  Proficiency in identifying and using comparative standards to estimate energy, fat, protein, carbohydrate, fiber, fluid, vitamin and mineral needs as well as recommended body weight, BMI, and desired growth patterns Required
•  Ability to be flexible and willingness to adapt to changes as necessary Required

Education
• Bachelor''s Required

Field of Study
• Divinity or Equiv

Experience
• N/A

